  { id: 3584, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:08:19Z", category: "bug", summary: "imp-3569 (bug): honesty-overclaim audit of the imp-3525..3532/3548 cohort per the imp-3459/imp-3480/imp-3499 pattern -- clean, zero leaks", files: ["src/data/imp-3569-honesty-overclaim-audit-3525-3532-3548.js"], detail: "Following the recurring honesty-audit pattern (imp-3459/imp-3480/imp-3499), audited the nine imp-3525/3526/3527/3528/3529/3530/3531/3532/3548 modules for accidental QED/RH-proof framing. Every module summary/verdict is free of QED/proves-RH/resolves-RH/closes-RH language, states RH-EQUIVALENT scope, NECESSARY-BUT-NOT-SUFFICIENT mass-feasibility, the imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED, and cites Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 as the rigorous SOTA. Per the sibling imp-3568 orphan audit none of the nine is actually import-ed by a page, but five (3527/3529/3530/3532/3548) have their findings independently re-stated by companion viz-data-driven pages whose rendered Honest status banners were checked and match. Zero leaks found; audit only, no data edits needed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3585, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:11:17Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3618 (numerical): extend the imp-3600/imp-3581 p=2 remainder-tail exponent ladder to rungs n=7 (odd sinh R_7) and n=8 (even cosh R_8), certifying closed C_7=M_9/(72 M_7), C_8=M_10/(90 M_8), D_7, D_8 and the fit-bias law", files: ["src/data/imp-3618-remainder-tail-exponent-ladder-n78.js"], detail: "Extends the imp-3600 certified n=5,6 rungs of the imp-3581 closed p=2 same-parity remainder tail derivation to n=7,8. Measures the A-weighted moments M_11..M_14 on the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson reference, computes the closed leading coefficients C_7=M_9/(72 M_7)~8.25809e-4 and C_8=M_10/(90 M_8)~7.39567e-4 (general C_n=M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n) at (8)(9)=72, (9)(10)=90) and the next-order D_7~-1.5787e-4, D_8~-1.3198e-4. Certifies the fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) reproduces the actual least-squares log-log slope to ~1e-9 (odd fitted 1.99999536, slopeModelErr~3.9e-10, |p-2|~4.64e-6; even fitted 1.99999214, slopeModelErr~6.6e-10, |p-2|~7.86e-6), r_n(a)/a^2->C_n at the deepest rung to 6.0e-10 (n=7) and 3.2e-8 (n=8), and both rungs stay on the monotone same-parity |p_fit-2| trend. Measurement/derivation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator positivity (imp-3066) untouched; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA; NO QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3586, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:12:54Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3620 (numerical): pin the imp-3604 N_half/N_x crossover ratio with the specific imp-398 backward-flow closed form t_c(N)=2.37e-4*log(gamma_N*)/log(gamma_N) (N*=1e4) instead of the flat flow-factor bracket endpoints", files: ["src/data/imp-3620-sigma-crossover-tc-closedform-pin.js"], detail: "imp-3604 bounded N_half/N_x under the whole flat Gronwall bracket [1,exp(4.74e-4)=1.000474] WITHOUT a specific t_c(N) closed form. This module derives the named imp-398 1/log gamma_N shrink -- t_c(N)=2.37e-4*log(gamma_N*)/log(gamma_N) with the N*=1e4 A1 anchor and gamma_N=effectiveHeightForN(N) -- and re-root-solves both crossings. At the crossover N_x=3.280294e9 the height log gamma is 2.27x the anchor, so t_c(N_x)=1.0452e-4 (0.441x the 2.37e-4 worst case) and the flow factor is pinned to 1.0001045 (C_G=1)..1.0002091 (C_G=2), landing at only 22.05%..44.09% of the imp-3604 bracket and BELOW the imp-3580 frozen 1.000237 (frozen over-states the amplification ~2.27x by never applying the shrink). The N_half/N_x ratio is thereby PINNED to a single per-floor value (band still [0.99313,0.99772]~0.996, f=1 reproducing imp-3580/imp-3604 0.996019 at N_x 3.280294e9) with only ~7.7e-7 residual C_G spread, tighter than the imp-3604 ~3e-6 flat-bracket spread; N_x and x(N_x)=1 unchanged (flow-free). Measurement/derivation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA; NO QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3587, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:14:23Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3619 (numerical): measure the THIRD skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 across N=160..2000 and test the imp-3602 j^2-1 amplitude law at pair j=4 (predicting -log sigma_3/-log rho -> a_4/a_2=5)", files: ["src/data/imp-3619-skew-toeplitz-third-gap-exponent.js"], detail: "Extends imp-3602 (which measured the second gap sigma_2=lambda_5/lambda_1 and reported the empirical amplitude law a_j proportional to j^2-1, tested only to pair j=3 via the single ratio -log sigma_2/-log rho ~ 8/3). Reuses the IDENTICAL imp-3505/imp-3575/imp-3602 Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R assembly (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) and full-reorthogonalization Lanczos with top-8 Ritz extraction at converged Krylov depth m=min(N,440), forming sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 across the imp-3555 ladder. FINDINGS: (1) the third gap converges to the SAME -2 section-gap heuristic -- global log-log fit q_3=-1.9817 (R^2=0.99999) matching q_1=-1.9811, local exponent climbing monotonically from -1.9568 (160->240) to -1.9948 (1600->2000), indistinguishable from the first gap (<3e-3). (2) The j^2-1 law HOLDS at pair j=4: -log sigma_3/-log rho tends to 5.00008 (mean 5.0022, spread 1.06e-2) matching a_4/a_2=(16-1)/(4-1)=5 to 8e-5, and independently -log sigma_3/-log sigma_2 -> 1.87502 matching a_4/a_3=15/8=1.875 -- two pair-ratios now corroborate the ordering. (3) lambda_7=lambda_8 pairing holds <4e-14 (<4e-11 at N=2000), a genuine fourth-pair level. Lower-gap -log sigma_2/-log rho reproduce the imp-3602 baked ladder to <3e-12 (same converged spectrum); every rung Krylov-locked vs m=400 to <6e-14. Measurement only; does NOT construct the missing magnitude, imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; RH-EQUIVALENT; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA; NO QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3588, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:15:14Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3617 (numerical): push the imp-3599 closed expansion of the exact flow-gap identity gap=1-(L_half/L_x)/(1+eta)^2 to O(eps^3), newly requiring the slope-curvature s=d2 lnL/d(lnN)2, and measure whether the residual shrinks toward the ~1e-13 exact floor", files: ["src/data/imp-3617-flow-gap-thirdorder-expansion.js", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3599 wrote the exact flow-gap identity gap=1-(L_half/L_x)/(1+eta)^2 (matching root-solved gaps to ~1e-14) and a crude O(eps^2) model 2 eps(1+lambda)-(4 mu+4 lambda+3) eps^2 that left a ~5% tail (imp-3599-nextorder-residual-tail, ~4.5e-4..1.9e-3 pp). This module expands the identity SELF-CONSISTENTLY as Du=ln(N_half/N_x)=d1 eps+d2 eps^2+d3 eps^3 by solving the fixed point Du=ln(L_half/L_x)-2 ln(1+eta) order by order: d1=-2/(1-lambda), d2=[(1/2)s d1^2+1-2 mu d1]/(1-lambda) (FIRST requiring the slope-curvature s=d2 lnL/d(lnN)2 and E_flow log-curvature nu=d2 lnE_flow/d(lnN)2), and d3 adding the log-N third derivative t; gap=1-exp(Du) truncated at each order. Re-root-solving both crossings per floor f in {0.5..2} (400-iter bisection, reproducing imp-3580/imp-3599) and evaluating the slopes by central FD in ln N (step 1e-4, stable under halving), the residual falls geometrically (per-order ratio ~100-500): resid_lead ~6.5e-5..5.1e-4, resid_O(eps^2) ~1.4e-7..3.3e-6, resid_O(eps^3) ~3.1e-10..2.3e-8 pp. The O(eps^3) truncation shrinks the imp-3599 O(eps^2) tail by 8.4e4..1.4e6x toward the ~1e-13 exact floor; the resummed leading d1=-2/(1-lambda) already beats the imp-3599 crude 2 eps(1+lambda) model (its dropped 2 lambda^2 eps piece is the dominant part of the tail). HONEST SUB-GAP imp-3617-fourthorder-fd-floor: the expansion does NOT reach the ~1e-13 exact floor -- a plateau at ~3e-10..2.3e-8 pp survives from the neglected O(eps^4) term and the finite-difference evaluation of s, nu, t. 7 assertions. Measurement/derivation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA; NO QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3590, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:15:51Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3570 (ux): add a Moment-Ladder Cluster Roundup panel to ClosureRoutesPage summarizing the imp-3481/3501/3502/3503/3526/3528/3532 autocorrelation moment-ladder + closed-error-certificate cluster verdicts and their shared imp-3066 obstruction", files: ["src/pages/ClosureRoutesPage.jsx"], detail: "Added MomentLadderClusterSummaryPanel, a new roundup table on ClosureRoutesPage (rendered directly after the existing MomentLadderResidualPanel) tabulating one-line verdicts for imp-3481 (the M_0..M_6 moment ladder as the Taylor ladder of the A-weighted cosh/sinh masses), imp-3501 (analytic all-n derivation, bit-for-bit match to the measured leading form), imp-3502 (fitted O(a^2) tail exponent per moment, worst deviation from 2), imp-3503 (Gauss-Legendre cross-validation to 6-7 sig figs), imp-3526 (cancellation-free R_4 sharpening the n=4 exponent), imp-3528 (closing the degree-4 Simpson-vs-GL gap with a converged M_4), and imp-3532 (the explicit closed error bound for all n), closing with a callout that none of them touch the shared imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel obstruction. Imports the six previously-orphaned modules (imp-3501/3502/3503/3526/3528/3532, per the imp-3568 surfacing audit) and pulls their live measured/certified constants rather than hardcoding them.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3591, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:20:38Z", category: "accuracy", summary: "imp-3621 (accuracy): bound the OUTER composite-Simpson truncation of the imp-3600 higher moments M_5..M_10 against an independent imp-3603-class Gauss-Legendre OUTER reference, certifying the p=2 exponent-ladder inputs carry no residual outer-quadrature bias", files: ["src/data/imp-3621-outer-simpson-truncation-moments-m5-m10.js"], detail: "imp-3603 removed Simpson from the inner A(tau) reference AND the outer moment weighting only for M_0..M_4; imp-3600 introduced M_5..M_10 on the NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson outer grid feeding the p=2 exponent ladder with no outer-truncation cross-check. Holding the inner rule identical on both paths (composite Simpson, INNER_N=1200 on [0,7]) so only the outer quadrature differs, this module re-weights tau^m A(tau) with a Gauss-Legendre OUTER rule (GL-24, 200 panels) and reports the per-moment relative gap. MEASURED: the GL outer reference self-converges to machine precision (GL-24/100 vs GL-24/200 ~1.05e-15); the outer-Simpson relative gap peaks at ~1.31e-10 (M_5) and falls to the ~1e-15 rounding floor for M_6..M_10 (M_6~3.9e-13, M_7~1.8e-13, M_8..M_10~1e-15), more than an order of magnitude below the imp-3600 ~1e-9 fit tolerance; and the C_5=M_7/(42 M_5)~1.06348e-3, C_6=M_8/(56 M_6), D_5, D_6 exponent-ladder brackets reconstructed from the Simpson-outer moments match the GL-outer ones to maxCoeffGap~5.89e-10 (<<1e-9). So the imp-3600 |p_fit-2| read-outs (~6.99e-6, ~1.14e-5) are the derived O(a^2) curvature bias, NOT outer-quadrature artifacts, extending the imp-3603 M_0..M_4 Simpson-free confirmation to the M_5..M_10 rungs imp-3600 actually feeds the ladder. 7 assertions. Cross-validation/measurement only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator positivity (imp-3066) untouched; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA; NO QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3592, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:21:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3622 (numerical): numerically CONFIRM the imp-3601 argmax-drift-0 discriminator against planted higher-order aliasing replicas by measuring the m-fold replica shift 2 m xi_Nyq per panel doubling", files: ["src/data/imp-3622-planted-replica-argmax-drift.js", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3601 DERIVED the m-fold aliasing fold-in ladder N_m=N_replica/m and ASSERTED (without measuring) that an m-fold replica shifts 2 m xi_Nyq per panel doubling. This module MEASURES it: it plants a synthetic feature at xi_true=250 (a sampled cosine on the imp-3558 midpoint nodes), whose discrete periodogram P_N is a Dirichlet comb peaking exactly at the imp-3601 image set {xi_true+2k xi_Nyq, 2 m xi_Nyq-xi_true}, and locates the first- (m=1) and second-fold (m=2) images by local fine scan (half-width 3, step 0.005) at the four rungs N in {1200,2400,4800,9600}. The measured images reproduce 2 m xi_Nyq-xi_true to <1e-6 (residual 0 on the aligned scan grid): first fold [1006.64,2263.27,4776.55,9803.10] moving 2 xi_Nyq(N) per doubling (across-ladder shift 8796.459, matches imp-3601 ~8797), second fold [2263.27,4776.55,9803.10,19856.19] moving 4 xi_Nyq(N) per doubling (across-ladder shift 17592.919, exactly 2x the first fold, matches ~17593). Meanwhile the genuine in-band feature keeps its argmax pinned at xi_true=250 at every rung (in-band drift ~1e-11) and BOTH replica images sit above the band ceiling xi_max=400 for every N>=1200 (smallest first-fold image 1006.64>400), so no fold lands in-band. The measured 0-vs-~8797/~17593 drift contrast IS the imp-3558 argmax-drift-0 discriminator, now confirmed on a planted feature of known frequency. 9 self-computing assertions; module registered in run-assertions.mjs. Measurement/certification only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; the imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity is UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3593, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:05:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3624 (numerical): measure the a-window sensitivity of the imp-3581/imp-3600 fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) -- confirm the closed law tracks the least-squares slope as the a-grid window is varied", files: ["src/data/imp-3624-fit-bias-a-window-sensitivity.js", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3600 certified p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) only on the fixed nine-rung (odd) / six-rung (even) a-ladders; its a-window dependence -- the very lever that makes the fitted exponent grid-dependent -- was untested. Across six distinct a-windows (varied lo/hi endpoints and rung counts; the covVar factor spanning ~0.00286 to ~0.05957, a ~20x range) for n=3..6, reusing the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson moments (no new moment computation), the fitted least-squares exponent MOVES by up to 2.23e-5 (n=3) between windows while the residual slopeModelErr=|p_fit-fitted| stays at the imp-3600 ~1e-9 level (global max 2.34e-9 across all 24 (n,window) cells). The extracted (fitted-2)/covVar recovers the closed D_n to <=1.08e-4 relative at every window, so D_n is window-invariant and the entire read-out drift IS the cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) term, not an unmodeled effect: the closed law tracks the slope as the a-window is varied, confirming the tail exponent is EXACTLY 2 and the sub-2 read-out is the derived O(a^2) curvature bias, window by window. 8 assertions; module registered in run-assertions.mjs. Measurement only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator positivity (imp-3066) UNTOUCHED; no RH verdict, no QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3594, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:22:04Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3583 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3558 four-rung far-tail xi* band-max grid ladder to N=9600, xi_Nyq~5027", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3558 extended the imp-3531 far-tail |P1| decade-band-max grid ladder one more doubling to N=9600 (xi_Nyq~5027), certifying the far-tail band-max Cauchy chain keeps shrinking on the new 4800->9600 leg (another ~16x) while the band argmax locations stay bit-identical across all four rungs (drift 0) against a hypothetical ~8797 Nyquist replica shift, and the far-tail ratio stays under 1% with monotone decay at every rung -- strengthening the imp-3511 no-missed-maximizer bound to a four-rung certificate. This module adds a glossary/concept entry summarizing the ladder, its aliasing-vs-genuine-decay discriminator, and its honest scope (measurement/certification only, xi* remains transcendental, no closed form, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED).", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3595, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:27:43Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3584 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3555 skew-Toeplitz gap-exponent convergence to the -2 section-gap heuristic", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3530 fit the skew-Toeplitz top-pair-degenerate Gram gap decay -log rho(N)=A N^q on N=160..800 and called q~-1.9725 merely near the -2 section-gap heuristic. imp-3555 extended the ladder with the imp-3545-measured N=1000/1200/1600 rungs and found the local pairwise log-log slope climbs monotonically toward -2 across every consecutive rung (-1.9540 at 160->240 through -1.9915 at 1000->1200, within 0.0086 of -2), the extended global OLS on the monotone N=160..1200 ladder sharpens to q=-1.9770 (R^2=0.99999, closer to -2 than the imp-3530 base), and the lone N=1600 rung is a non-monotone measurement artifact (naively included it collapses the fit to q=-1.763, R^2 0.9605) rather than genuine exponent drift. Added a new glossary entry documenting the convergence, the sharpened extended fit, and the isolated N=1600 artifact. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3596, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:28:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3625 (numerical): assess whether the imp-3602 lambda_5=lambda_6 third-pair degeneracy loss at deep N (2e-14 -> 1.01e-11 at Krylov depth m=440) is a Lanczos KRYLOV reorthogonalization limit that deeper reorth depth restores in the imp-3575 manner", files: ["src/data/imp-3625-skew-toeplitz-pair56-krylov-depth.js", "scripts/compute-imp3625-pair56-krylov.mjs", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3602 reported the third-pair degeneracy lambda_5=lambda_6 holding to relative <2e-14 through N=1200 but LOOSENING to 1.01e-11 at N=2000 -- all at a fixed Lanczos Krylov depth m=440 -- the same qualitative signature imp-3575 traced to an m=200 lambda_3 under-resolution deficit that grows with N. Re-running the IDENTICAL imp-3505/imp-3575/imp-3596/imp-3602 assembly Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) at N=2000 with a single full-reorthogonalization Lanczos to m=640 and reading the top-6 Gram Ritz values at m in {440,480,560,640} (leading tridiagonal sub-blocks): at the imp-3602 depth m=440 the third-pair splitting pair56=|sigma_5-sigma_6|/sigma_5=1.0102e-11 reproduces the imp-3602 baked value (1.010245749617736e-11) to 6 significant figures (self-check of the assembly), but growing to m=480 CONTRACTS pair56 ~1667x to 6.06e-15 and it stays at the <2e-14 machine floor for all deeper depths (m=560: 1.88e-14, m=640: 7.31e-15), returning to the level imp-3602 saw at every rung through N=1200 -- NOT flooring at 1.01e-11. So lambda_5=lambda_6 is genuinely degenerate at N=2000 too and the imp-3602 m=440 pair56 was Krylov-UNDER-resolved: EXACTLY the imp-3575 pattern one gap and one ladder-rung deeper (lambda_3 under-resolved at (1600,200), locking at m>=280; lambda_5=lambda_6 under-resolved at (2000,440), locking at m>=480), i.e. higher reorthogonalized Krylov depth RESTORES the degeneracy in the imp-3575 manner rather than the loss being a genuine near-degeneracy splitting. Crucially the second gap sigma_2=lambda_5/lambda_1=0.99958651049280 is INVARIANT across m=440..640 to relative ~2e-14 (three orders below the 1e-11 loss), so the m=440 pair56 under-resolution did NOT corrupt the imp-3602 second-gap value or its q_2=-1.9813 exponent. 6 self-checking assertions; module registered in run-assertions.mjs; offline compute script scripts/compute-imp3625-pair56-krylov.mjs reproduces the Ritz literals (~50 s). Measurement only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; the imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity is UNTOUCHED; NO RH verdict, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3597, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:15:00Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3585 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3556 conditional-share crossing-spacing odds-ratio law and its logistic-in-lnN sigma-drop profile", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3556 root-solved the six post-peak sigma(N)=E_coll/E(N) threshold crossings and derived the cancellation-free odds-ratio spacing law N=K*logT0(N)*((1-sigma)/sigma)^2, K=(C_C_PINNED/E_trunc)^2=1.5727e8, matching the exact roots with relative error equal to the neglected E_flow term; it also corrected the imp-3529 loose ~0.4-per-decade phrasing, showing the sigma-drop is a logistic-in-lnN profile peaking 0.2738/decade exactly at the E_coll=E_trunc crossover (below the ln10/8=0.2879 cap) and vanishing at both the flat interior maximum and the far tail. Added a new glossary entry documenting the odds-ratio spacing law, the ~1-decade interior crossing spacing, and the logistic drop profile, cross-linked to imp-3529/imp-3444/imp-3463. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3598, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:39:53Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3586 (ux): add a visualization page for the imp-3556 post-peak sigma(N) crossings and the logistic sigma-drop profile", files: ["src/pages/Imp3586SigmaCrossingLogisticDropViz.jsx", "src/data/imp-3586-sigma-crossing-logistic-drop-viz-data.js", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3556 root-solved the six post-peak sigma(N)=E_coll/E(N) threshold crossings (sigma<0.9,0.75,0.5,0.25,0.1,0.01; log10 N 7.41..13.67) and quantified the sigma-drop rate -dsigma/dlog10N as a logistic-in-lnN bump peaking at 0.2738/decade near the E_coll=E_trunc crossover (sigma~0.4957), under the untrimmed logistic cap ln10/8=0.28782 -- but that measurement had no page consumer. Added a new lightweight viz-data module (baked reference literals reproduced from the imp-3556 CROSSINGS/dropPerDecade fields, no heavy re-computation on import) and a page rendering two SVG charts: the sigma(N) post-peak curve with the six root-solved crossings marked, and the logistic drop profile with the peak and the ln10/8 cap drawn. Wired the route /viz-imp3586-sigma-crossing-logistic-drop into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3563..3567 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3599, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:44:23Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3587 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3550 Euler-Maclaurin midpoint ANALYTIC O(H^2) far-tail band-max error bound, upgrading the imp-3531 EMPIRICAL Cauchy ladder to an a-priori 4x-per-doubling envelope", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3531 certified the imp-3511 far-tail |P1| decade-band-max grid ladder converged but flagged the convergence as an EMPIRICAL Cauchy/O(H^2) observation over a finite ladder, not an analytic error bound. imp-3550 closed that gap by deriving the composite-midpoint Euler-Maclaurin remainder for the four P1 sub-integrals and delivering |bandMax_N - bandMax_exact| <= B_band*H^2, a rigorous-but-conservative bound under which halving H shrinks the certified error EXACTLY 4x and the imp-3531 empirical leg change sits under the analytic envelope. Added a new glossary entry summarizing the derivation, the exact 4x shrink signature, and the honest scope (conservative bound, xi* stays transcendental, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3600, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:52:00Z", category: "accuracy", summary: "imp-3623 (accuracy): dense-solver cross-validate the imp-3602 second gap sigma_2=lambda_5/lambda_1 at deep N=1200/1600/2000 against an independent Householder+QL dense full-spectrum solver, certifying the imp-3602 N=2000 lambda_5=lambda_6 degeneracy loss is a Krylov reorthogonalization artifact", files: ["src/data/imp-3623-skew-toeplitz-second-gap-dense-crossval.js", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3602 read the second skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_2=lambda_5/lambda_1 off a full-reorthogonalization Lanczos at Krylov depth m=min(N,440) and flagged the lambda_5=lambda_6 pair degeneracy DEGRADING from <2e-14 to ~1.01e-11 at the deepest N=2000 rung, leaving open whether the deep sigma_2 and that degeneracy loss were faithful or Lanczos-specific. This module reuses the identical imp-3505/imp-3596/imp-3602 assembly Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint), forms the Gram S=T^T T explicitly at the deep rungs N in {1200,1600,2000}, and computes the whole symmetric spectrum with an INDEPENDENT dense full-spectrum eigensolver (Householder tridiagonalization + implicit-QL: all eigenvalues, NO Krylov subspace, NO reorthogonalization, so it cannot host a Lanczos ghost). RESULT: (1) the dense sigma_2 reproduces the imp-3602 Lanczos value to relative <2.1e-14 at every deep rung (1.18e-14/8.44e-15/2.03e-14), so the deepest imp-3602 sigma_2=0.999586510492813 is a faithful reading; (2) the dense spectrum is adjacent-paired to <1.2e-15 at every rung, and CRUCIALLY the dense lambda_5=lambda_6 spread at N=2000 is 1.18e-15 (machine precision) vs the imp-3602 Lanczos 1.01e-11 (~10^4 larger) -- so the N=2000 degeneracy loss is a Krylov reorthogonalization artifact of the m=440 depth, not a genuine near-degeneracy splitting, and lambda_5 is a genuine third-pair level at N=2000; (3) the same dense solve recovers the imp-3575/imp-3596 converged first gap rho at N=1600 (rel 1.15e-14). Householder+QL was cross-checked to reproduce the imp-3596 cyclic-Jacobi top-6 at the shared N=80 to 2.29e-14; deep-rung dense top-6 measured offline (N=2000 solve ~36 s) and baked import-light with ratios/pairing self-checking. 7 assertions; module registered in run-assertions.mjs. Cross-validation/measurement only, RH-EQUIVALENT, imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity untouched, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3601, timestamp: "2026-07-03T12:50:09Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3588 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3552 cosh-certificate over-estimation factor F_n(a)=cosh(a T_A)/S_n(a), closed ceiling 1<=F_n<=cosh(a T_A)", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3532 promoted the imp-3501 moment-tail residual to the closed sharp cosh(a T_A) certificate but only checked the bound holds; imp-3546 measured the reciprocal ratio tending to 1 in the small-a limit without quantifying the over-estimation across the full imp-3532 a-ladder. imp-3552 supplies that profile: writing the exact residual tail as its leading term times a residual-shape factor, the over-estimation factor F_n(a)=cosh(a T_A)/S_n(a) factors cleanly, giving the closed ceiling 1<=F_n(a)<=cosh(a T_A). Measured across a in {0.5,0.25,0.125,0.0625}, rungs n=0..4: F_n(a) is ~10.06 at a=0.5 (matching cosh 3), ~2.35 at a=0.25, ~1.29 at a=0.125, ~1.07 at a=0.0625, dominated by the cosh inflation constant since the shape factor stays within 0.045% of 1. Added a new glossary entry summarizing this profile and its honest scope (measurement/certification only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3602, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:57:00Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3589 (ux): add a visualization page for the imp-3552 cosh-certificate over-estimation factor F_n(a) collapsing across the a-ladder against the cosh(a T_A) ceiling", files: ["src/pages/Imp3589CoshOverestimationFactorViz.jsx", "src/data/imp-3589-cosh-overestimation-factor-viz-data.js", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3552 measured the imp-3532 sharp cosh(a T_A) certificate's over-estimation factor F_n(a)=bound_sharp/|E_n(a)| across the a-ladder a in {0.5,0.25,0.125,0.0625} for rungs n=0..4, showing F_n(a) collapses from ~10.06 (a=0.5) to ~1.07 (a=0.0625) while hugging the cosh(a T_A) ceiling to within 0.05% -- but that measurement had no page consumer. Added a new lightweight viz-data module (baked reference literals reproduced from the imp-3552 measured.profile field, no heavy re-computation on import) and a page rendering one log-log SVG chart: the five F_n(a) polylines (n=0..4) plotted against a continuous cosh(a T_A) dashed envelope, visually showing the ladder hugging the ceiling. Wired the route /viz-imp3589-cosh-overestimation-factor into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3563..3567/3586 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3603, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:02:48Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3590 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3551 SHARPENED xi*_inf quadrature residual band 1e-6 -> 1e-9", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3548 confirmed xi*_inf is quadrature-scheme-invariant across an order-10 composite Gauss-Legendre rule and a trapezoid+Richardson limit, but explicitly declined to sharpen the residual band, which stayed quoted at the imp-3523 CONSERVATIVE 1e-6 even though its own converged Gauss-Legendre tail moved by under 1e-8. imp-3551 recomputed the extrapolation-free composite 5-point Gauss-Legendre ladder (N=45..720) with no extrapolation model, measured the converged-tail bit-stability spread over N>=90 at ~6.5e-10, and certified a SHARPENED band as the smallest clean decade strictly above that spread: 1e-9, 1000x tighter than before, corroborated by trapezoid+Richardson agreement to ~1e-15. Added a new glossary entry summarizing this sharpening, the measured convergence ladder, and the honest scope (measurement/certification only, xi* stays transcendental, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3604, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:05:00Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3591 (ux): re-point the imp-3563 quadrature-straddle viz's surfaced xi*_inf residual band from the CONSERVATIVE imp-3523/imp-3548 1e-6 to the imp-3551 SHARPENED 1e-9", files: ["src/pages/Imp3563QuadratureStraddleViz.jsx"], detail: "imp-3551 sharpened the xi*_inf quadrature-convergence residual band from the imp-3523/imp-3548 conservative 1e-6 to a measured 1e-9 (three independent numerical routes agree to ~1e-9 or better), but the imp-3563 quadrature-straddle visualization's honest-status caption still told readers the trapezoid-Richardson/Gauss-Legendre agreement landed inside the stale conservative 1e-6 band. Grepped all pages/components/paper-meta for consumer-facing text quoting the 1e-6 band and found this was the only surfaced instance (the imp-3523/imp-3548/imp-3572 data modules describe the band historically and were left untouched per scope). Updated the caption text to cite the imp-3551 SHARPENED 1e-9 band so the surfaced uncertainty matches the measured three-route agreement. Presentation-only text change; RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3605, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:11:08Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3592 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3553 CANCELLATION-FREE odd degree-3 remainder R_3(a)=sum_{m odd>=3} a^m/m! M_m", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3526 reformulated the even degree-4 remainder R_4 as a positive moment series to remove its M_0*eps cancellation floor; imp-3553 extended that reformulation to the odd degree-3 remainder R_3 (sinh), writing R_3(a)=S(a)-a M_1=sum_{m odd>=3} a^m/m! M_m as a strictly positive sum with no subtraction of near-equal masses, giving a clean O(a^2) residual tail with no rounding floor. It also corrected the frontier-scout premise that odd R_3 loses ladder rungs identically to even R_4: R_3 subtracts only a M_1 (~2.3e-5) versus R_4's M_0 (~7.7e-4), so its cancellation floor sits ~34x lower and it survives three octaves deeper before breaking down. The recovered nine-rung ladder gives a cancellation-free fit p=1.99999 (R^2=0.99999999996) against the corrupted subtractive fit p=1.85615 (R^2=0.98499), confirming R_3(a)=(a^3/6)M_3+O(a^5) at the derived order p=2. Added a new glossary entry documenting the reformulation, the odd-vs-even floor asymmetry, and the honest scope (measurement/certification only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3606, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:17:51Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3593 (meta): audit whether the imp-3462/3546/3547/3550/3551/3552/3553/3555/3556/3557/3558 research modules are imported by any page/component consumer or are orphaned data files", files: ["src/data/imp-3593-3546-3558-3462-cohort-module-surfacing-audit.js"], detail: "imp-3539 audited through imp-3511 and imp-3568 audited through imp-3532/3548, leaving the newest wave imp-3462 (N_max exponent derivation), imp-3546 (moment-tail bound tightness), imp-3547 (lower-moment Simpson residual localization), imp-3550 (far-tail midpoint O(H^2) bound), imp-3551 (xi*_inf band sharpening), imp-3552 (cosh over-estimation factor), imp-3553 (cancellation-free odd R_3), imp-3555 (skew-Toeplitz gap exponent convergence), imp-3556 (sigma threshold crossings), imp-3557 (M_4 leading-form propagation), and imp-3558 (far-tail N=9600 ladder) unaudited. Ran a transitive import-graph walk from every src/pages and src/components entry point over real relative `from` import edges (comment/@fileoverview mentions do not count). Found all eleven modules are ORPHAN: only imp-3546 has any real downstream import edge at all (from imp-3573 and imp-3574), and both of those importers are themselves unreached from any page or component, confirming the imp-3568 finding that this whole research-module chain has not been wired into a live page. Recorded per-module surfaced/orphan status plus a recommendation grouping follow-up surfacing tickets by narrative home (N_max/rescue-budget, moment-ladder/xi* quadrature, remainder-tail exponent, section-gap/sigma-crossover, miss-factor refinement, far-tail band-max). Read-only audit; no pages fabricated; RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3607, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:20:03Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3638 (numerical): extend the imp-3618/imp-3581 p=2 remainder-tail exponent ladder to n=9 (odd sinh R_9) and n=10 (even cosh R_10) -- C_9=M_11/(110 M_9)~6.68e-4, C_10=M_12/(132 M_10)~6.08e-4, D_9~-1.12e-4, D_10~-9.58e-5, fit-bias law reproduces slope to ~2.5e-10/4.3e-10", files: ["src/data/imp-3638-remainder-tail-exponent-ladder-n910.js"], detail: "imp-3618 certified the closed C_n=M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n) form only through n=7,8. This module measures the A-weighted moments M_15..M_18 on the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson reference, reconstructs C_9=M_11/(110 M_9)~6.67939e-4, C_10=M_12/(132 M_10)~6.07591e-4 and the next-order D_9~-1.1181e-4, D_10~-9.582e-5, and confirms the imp-3581 fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) still reproduces the actual least-squares log-log slope (odd fitted 1.99999671 vs predicted 1.99999671, slopeModelErr~2.5e-10, |p-2|~3.29e-6; even fitted 1.99999429 vs predicted 1.99999429, slopeModelErr~4.3e-10, |p-2|~5.71e-6), well inside the imp-3600 ~1e-9 tolerance. Both new rungs stay on the monotone same-parity |p_fit-2| trend (odd 1.16e-5,6.99e-6,4.64e-6,3.29e-6; even 1.80e-5,1.14e-5,7.86e-6,5.71e-6) and r_n(a)/a^2 confirms C_n independently (4.3e-10, 2.3e-8). MEASUREMENT/DERIVATION only, RH-equivalent, necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 untouched; no QED; 10 self-computing assertions pass; build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3608, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:40:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3639 (numerical): DERIVE the imp-3602/imp-3619 EMPIRICAL skew-Toeplitz a_j proportional to (j^2-1) amplitude law as the UNIQUE ratio signature of a Dirichlet-Laplacian effective operator mu_k=C k^2, uniquely selected against k / 2k-1 / k(k+1)", files: ["src/data/imp-3639-skew-toeplitz-amplitude-law-derivation.js"], detail: "imp-3602/imp-3619 measured the skew-Toeplitz Gram gaps -log(lambda_{2j-1}/lambda_1) of Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R(|v-u|) and flagged the pair-index amplitude law a_j proportional to (j^2-1) (ratios a_3/a_2=8/3, a_4/a_2=5, a_4/a_3=15/8, tested to j=4) as EMPIRICAL, not derived. This module reduces BOTH the -2 section-gap exponent (E1) and the (j^2-1) ordering (E3) to a SINGLE structural hypothesis: the finite-section splitting on [0,U] (U=N H0) is governed at leading order by a Sturm-Liouville / Dirichlet-Laplacian effective operator with spectrum mu_k=C k^2 (C proportional to U^-2=N^-2), the skew (v-u) factor doubling each level so pair j maps to k=j and -log(lambda_{2j-1}/lambda_1)=mu_j-mu_1=C(j^2-1). C proportional to N^-2 gives the -2 exponent for every pair, and C cancels in every pair-ratio, giving the closed a_j/a_2=(j^2-1)/3 => 8/3, 5, 15/8, matching the imp-3619 measured ratios to ~1e-4 at N=2000 (2.66668, 5.00008, 1.87502). DISCRIMINATING TEST: among the natural second-order index ladders (k, 2k-1, k(k+1), k^2) ONLY the k^2 Dirichlet-Laplacian ladder reproduces all three measured ratios (k and 2k-1 give 2,3,3/2; k(k+1) gives 5/2,9/2,9/5), so the ordering is FORCED, not one fit among many. HONEST PARTIAL DERIVATION: the ordering is derived up to the effective-operator hypothesis (uniquely selected by the data); NOT derived are the symbol-to-operator identity (section reduces EXACTLY to mu_k=(k pi/U)^2) and the absolute constant C (the imp-3066 missing magnitude, which cancels in ratios) -- named sub-gap sg-3639-effective-operator-identity. 7 self-checking assertions run on import; import-light closed-form arithmetic, no heavy assembly re-run. RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3609, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:23:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3641 (numerical): push the imp-3617 self-consistent flow-gap expansion to O(eps^4) -- DERIVE d4 order-by-order and MEASURE whether resid4 approaches the ~1e-13 exact-identity floor across the imp-3443 f in {0.5..2} floor grid", files: ["src/data/imp-3641-flow-gap-fourthorder-expansion.js"], detail: "imp-3617 pushed the exact flow-gap identity gap=1-(L_half/L_x)/(1+eta)^2 to a self-consistent O(eps^3) closed expansion Du=ln(N_half/N_x)=d1 eps+d2 eps^2+d3 eps^3, driving the residual to ~3e-10..2.3e-8 pp but leaving the sub-gap imp-3617-fourthorder-fd-floor above the ~1e-13 exact floor. This module DERIVES the O(eps^4) coefficient d4 order-by-order from the same fixed point Du=ln(L_half/L_x)-2 ln(1+eta), FIRST requiring the 4th log-N derivative q=d^4 lnL/d(lnN)^4 and the 3rd E_flow log derivative rho=d^3 lnE_flow/d(lnN)^3: d4=[s d1 d3+(1/2)s d2^2+(1/2)t d1^2 d2+(1/24)q d1^4-2 mu d3-2(mu^2+nu)d1 d2-((1/3)mu^3+mu nu+(1/3)rho)d1^3+2 mu d2+(2 mu^2+nu)d1^2-2 mu d1+1/2]/(1-lambda), with gap4=gap3-(d4+d1 d3+(1/2)d2^2+(1/2)d1^2 d2+(1/24)d1^4)eps^4. Re-root-solving both crossings per floor (reproducing imp-3617 to the last digit) and evaluating q, rho at a ROBUST step h4=1e-2 (a 4th derivative at the imp-3617 step h=1e-4 has numerator noise ~h^4=1e-16, i.e. pure roundoff), resid4 improves resid3 at EVERY floor by 13..309x to the ~2e-11..7e-10 pp band. Crucially, at the naive h=1e-4 step q collapses to roundoff garbage (0, +-17.8), corrupting the (1/24)q d1^4 term of d4 and making resid4 WORSE than resid3 at f>=1 (up to 1.7e-7 pp) -- the concrete finite-difference floor of the 4th derivative. d4~-11.0..-11.8 is dominated by products of the lower derivatives; the genuinely new q~-1.5e-5..-2.3e-5 and rho~5e-4..7e-4 are small and contribute sub-1e-3 to d4. HONEST EXTENDED SUB-GAP imp-3641-fifthorder-fd-floor: the O(eps^4) expansion does NOT reach the ~1e-13 exact floor; a plateau survives from the O(eps^5) term and the finite-difference evaluation of q. 7 self-computing assertions pass on import. MEASUREMENT/DERIVATION only, RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3610, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:22:46Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3640 (numerical): measure the FOURTH skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_4=lambda_9/lambda_1 across N=160..2000 and confirm the imp-3619 (j^2-1) amplitude law prediction a_5/a_2=(25-1)/(4-1)=8", files: ["src/data/imp-3640-skew-toeplitz-fourth-gap-exponent.js", "scripts/compute-imp3640-fourth-gap.mjs"], detail: "imp-3619 measured the third gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 and corroborated the empirical amplitude law a_j proportional to (j^2-1) through pair j=4, leaving the next prediction a_5/a_2=8 for the FIFTH pair (lambda_9=lambda_10) untested. Re-ran the IDENTICAL imp-3505/imp-3575/imp-3619 skew-Toeplitz assembly (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) with a single full-reorthogonalization Lanczos at a depth that grows with N (m=min(N,560) at N=2000, mind the imp-3625 depth-vs-N under-resolution), extracting the top-10 Gram Ritz values across the 11-rung ladder. The fourth gap converges to the SAME -2 section-gap heuristic (global q_4=-1.9822, R^2=0.99999, matching q_1=-1.9811 to 1.15e-3; local exponent climbs monotonically -1.9588 -> -1.9948, tracking q_1 to <5e-3), and the amplitude ratio -log sigma_4/-log rho tends CLEANLY to 8 (8.0296 at N=160 -> 8.00022 at N=2000, mean 8.0060) matching a_5/a_2=8 to 2.2e-4, with two further independent checks -log sigma_4/-log sigma_2 -> 3.00006=a_5/a_3 and -log sigma_4/-log sigma_3 -> 1.60002=a_5/a_4=8/5. This is the direct empirical corroboration at j=5 of the imp-3639 Dirichlet-Laplacian mu_k=C k^2 derivation. The lambda_9=lambda_10 pairing holds to <2e-14 at every rung (genuine fifth-pair level, not a ghost), every rung Krylov-locks to <4e-14, and the third/second/first-gap -log literals reproduce the imp-3619 baked ladder to <3e-12 (same converged spectrum). So the j^2-1 ordering, corroborated through pair j=4, is now confirmed at j=5 by three pair-ratios, extending the -2 heuristic across the top FIVE pairs. MEASUREMENT only; empirical not derived; RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 K_a>=0 untouched; NO QED; 8 self-computing assertions pass; build passes. Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3611, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:45:00Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3594 (meta): honesty-audit the imp-3462/3546/3547/3550/3551/3552/3553/3555/3556/3557/3558 cohort for false-QED or RH-overclaim framing per the imp-3459/imp-3480/imp-3499 pattern -- all eleven modules carry a compliant banner (measurement/derivation only, RH-equivalent or explicit no-RH-verdict scope, imp-3066 untouched, Platt-Trudgian SOTA cited, no QED); zero flags", files: ["src/data/imp-3594-3462-3558-cohort-honesty-banner-audit.js"], detail: "Following the imp-3499/imp-3459/imp-3569/imp-3593 honesty-audit pattern, re-read the @fileoverview banner and exported verdict/note field of each of the eleven imp-3462/3546/3547/3550/3551/3552/3553/3555/3556/3557/3558 modules for measurement/derivation-only framing, RH-EQUIVALENT (or explicit no-RH-verdict) scope, the imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel K_a>=0 positivity obstruction marked UNTOUCHED, Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 cited as the rigorous SOTA, and absence of QED/unconditional-RH phrasing. Every module already carries all five markers (imp-3462 and imp-3556 phrase it as \"no positivity, no bridge closure, no RH claim, NO QED\" since their topics are pure exponent/threshold measurements with no imp-3066 tie-in claimed; the other nine explicitly name imp-3066 untouched). None of the derivation framings (imp-3462 closed-form exponent, imp-3550 analytic O(H^2) bound, imp-3555 skew-Toeplitz exponent convergence) reads as a rigorous closure step. Cross-checked against the imp-3593 page-surfacing audit: all eleven remain orphan, so no reader-facing page could currently be misled by an under-scoped banner. Read-only audit; no pages fabricated, no modules edited; 3 self-computing assertions pass; RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3612, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:29:08Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3644 (numerical): extend the imp-3621 outer-Simpson truncation bound from M_5..M_10 to the higher moments M_11..M_14 that imp-3618 feeds the n=7,8 exponent ladder -- per-moment Simpson-vs-GL-outer relative gap at the ~1e-15 rounding floor (max ~2.2e-15 at M_13), C_7/C_8/D_7/D_8 ladder inputs outer-rule-invariant to <<1e-9", files: ["src/data/imp-3644-outer-simpson-truncation-moments-m11-m14.js"], detail: "imp-3621 bounded the OUTER composite-Simpson truncation of M_5..M_10 (max relative gap ~1.31e-10 at M_5, rounding-floor for M_6..M_10) against the imp-3603 Gauss-Legendre OUTER reference, but imp-3618 then introduced the higher moments M_11..M_14 on the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson outer grid to form C_7=M_9/(72 M_7), C_8=M_10/(90 M_8) and the next-order D_7, D_8 brackets for the n=7,8 rungs of the p=2 exponent ladder, with no outer-truncation cross-check. Holding the inner rule identical (composite Simpson INNER_N=1200 on [0,7]) on both paths so ONLY the outer quadrature differs, MEASURED |M_m^Simpson - M_m^GL|/|M_m^GL| for m=11..14 against a panel-doubling-certified GL-24/200 outer reference: the GL reference self-converges to ~1.4e-15 (GL-24/100 vs 200); every M_11..M_14 gap sits at the ~1e-15 rounding floor (max ~2.2e-15 at M_13), EVEN FURTHER below the ~1e-9 fit tolerance than the imp-3621 M_5..M_10 peak, because the tau^m weight concentrates in the smooth interior of [0,T_A] as m grows and the outer-Simpson O(h^4) truncation collapses to rounding; and the C_7, C_8, D_7, D_8 exponent-ladder brackets reconstructed from the Simpson-outer moments match the GL-outer ones to <<1e-9 (max ~9.5e-13 at D_7). So the imp-3618 |p_fit-2| read-outs (~4.64e-6, ~7.86e-6) are the derived O(a^2) curvature bias, NOT an outer-quadrature artifact, extending the imp-3621 M_5..M_10 confirmation to the M_11..M_14 rungs imp-3618 actually feeds the n=7,8 ladder. 8 self-computing assertions pass on import; import-light closed-form quadrature, no heavy assembly. CROSS-VALIDATION/MEASUREMENT only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3613, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:29:56Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3643 (numerical): dense-solver cross-validate the imp-3619 THIRD skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 at the deep rungs N in {1200,1600,2000} against the independent Householder+implicit-QL dense full-spectrum solver, certifying lambda_7 is a genuine FOURTH-pair level and the N=2000 Lanczos pair78 loss is a Krylov artifact", files: ["src/data/imp-3643-skew-toeplitz-third-gap-dense-crossval.js", "scripts/imp-3643-dense-third-gap-offline.mjs"], detail: "imp-3619 read sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 off a full-reorthogonalization Lanczos at m=min(N,440) only, and its lambda_7=lambda_8 pair degeneracy degraded from <4e-14 to ~3.99e-11 at the deepest N=2000 rung; imp-3623 dense-certified only the SECOND gap (top-6) and imp-3596 only the first at reduced sections, so the deep sigma_3 and the fourth-pair degeneracy were never checked against a non-Lanczos solver. Reusing the IDENTICAL imp-3505/imp-3619/imp-3623 assembly Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint), the offline script forms the Gram S=T^T T EXPLICITLY at N in {1200,1600,2000} and runs the SAME independent dense full-spectrum route imp-3623 used (Householder tridiagonalization tred1 + implicit-QL tql1: all eigenvalues, no Krylov subspace, no reorthogonalization), extended to the TOP-EIGHT eigenvalues to reach lambda_7=lambda_8 (N=2000 solve ~5 s). RESULT: (1) the dense sigma_3 reproduces the imp-3619 Lanczos value to <3.5e-14 at every deep rung (1.22e-14 at 1200, 3.43e-14 at 1600, 1.00e-15 at 2000), so the deepest sigma_3=0.9992248404950668 is solver-independent; (2) the dense spectrum is FOUR-pair adjacent-paired to <2.75e-15 at every rung, and CRUCIALLY the dense lambda_7=lambda_8 spread at N=2000 is 1.96e-16 (machine precision) while the imp-3619 Lanczos spread was 3.99e-11 (~2e5 larger) -- so the N=2000 pair78 loss is a Krylov reorthogonalization artifact of the m=440 depth, NOT a genuine splitting, and lambda_7 is a genuine fourth-pair level at N=2000; (3) the dense top-6 here reproduce the imp-3623 baked deep top-6 to all printed digits and the dense first gap rho at N=1600 (0.9997579854030993) recovers the imp-3575/imp-3623 converged rho=0.9997579854030878 to rel 1.15e-14. Deep-rung dense top-8 measured offline and BAKED; ratios/four-pair pairing self-check at import (7 self-computing assertions pass). CROSS-VALIDATION only; does NOT construct the missing magnitude and does NOT attempt the imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity; RH-EQUIVALENT; NO RH verdict, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3614, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:52:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3645 (numerical): unify the imp-3575 lambda_3 (N=1600, m*=280) and imp-3625 lambda_5=lambda_6 (N=2000, m*=480) converged-Krylov-depth anchors and fit m*(N) -- form is UNDER-determined by two heterogeneous anchors and the growth is a PAIR-INDEX confound, not an N-law", files: ["src/data/imp-3645-skew-toeplitz-krylov-depth-vs-N-law.js"], detail: "The ticket posits m*(N) as a single N-growth law across the imp-3575 lambda_3 lock (m>=280 at N=1600) and the imp-3625 lambda_5=lambda_6 lock (m>=480 at N=2000). Unifying the two already-measured anchors (no new Lanczos), the fit is UNDER-determined: two points fit any two-parameter form (linear/sqrt/log) exactly with zero residual, so linear vs sqrt vs log is not discriminated. The named 280->480 rise is a factor 1.714 while N rises only 1.25 (super-linear in N, far above sqrt(N)=1.118); a genuine fixed-pair Lanczos interior-eigenvalue depth grows at most ~N, so the jump is driven by the PAIR INDEX (2->3), not N. The homogeneous same-pair (lambda_3, pair 2) evidence confirms it: imp-3575 locked lambda_3 at m<=200 (N=1200), m=280 (N=1600), m=280 (N=2000) -- FLAT at 280 across N=1600..2000. Extrapolating the two-point fits gives at N=2400 linear 680/sqrt 661/log 643 (~5.7 pct spread) and at N=3200 linear 1080/sqrt 982/log 901 (~19.8 pct spread), trustworthy one rung out only; conservative engineering floor m>=~680 (N=2400), m>=~1080 (N=3200). NAMED SUB-GAP sg-3645-matched-pair-depth-sweep: discriminating the form needs a matched-pair sweep (fixed pair index, >=3 values of N) to separate pair-index from N. 7 self-computing assertions pass. Measurement/fit only; runs no new Lanczos; RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3615, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:30:29Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3605 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3575 skew-Toeplitz N=1600 gap non-monotonicity being a Krylov-truncation deficit, not a genuine gap reversal", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3555 flagged the N=1600 rung of the skew-Toeplitz gap ladder as a non-monotone data-quality outlier without testing why. imp-3575 re-measured rho=lambda_3/lambda_1 at N=1600 (and the new N=2000) with the Lanczos Krylov depth grown past the imp-3545 m=200 reference, finding the m=200 rho=0.9993548 was still climbing in lambda_3 (jumps +4.03e-4 to 0.9997580 at m=240, then LOCKS), while the N=1200 anchor was already converged at m=200 -- an N-specific truncation deficit matching the imp-3505/imp-3537 pattern. The corrected -log rho(N) ladder is strictly decreasing through N=2000 and the local log-log slope continues the imp-3555 climb toward -2 (-1.9933, -1.9949). Added a new glossary entry documenting the correction and its honest scope (measurement only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3616, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:34:47Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3642 (numerical): direct backward-Dyson RK4 cross-check of the imp-3620/imp-398 1/log gamma_N crossover-scale flow factor -- the direct flow reproduces the 1/log SHAPE (V0 linear in log(gamma/2pi)) but the anchor-to-crossover shrink is 0.3870 (density-log) not the assumed 0.4410 (bare height log), so imp-398 over-states t_c(N_x) by ~13.96%", files: ["src/data/imp-3642-sigma-crossover-tc-direct-dyson-crosscheck.js"], detail: "imp-3620 DERIVED the crossover-scale flow factor from the NAMED imp-398 t_c(N)~1/log gamma_N law, pinning t_c(N_x)=2.37e-4*0.4410=1.0452e-4 and the C_G=1 flow factor to 1.0001045, but that 1/log SHAPE and 0.4410 factor were ASSERTED from the heuristic, never checked against a direct flow integration. This module runs the direct check: it seeds a locally-uniform mesoscopic gas at the Riemann-von Mangoldt local density d=2pi/log(gamma/2pi) across a ladder of heights (anchor gamma_N*=effectiveHeightForN(1e4), log=9.1981, to crossover gamma_Nx=exp(20.8576)), integrates the attractive Calogero-Moser Step-2 backward-Dyson flow dx_k/ds=-2 sum 1/(x_k-x_j) by RK4 over half the shock budget [0,1/(4 V0)] (safely pre-collision), and measures the mesoscopic density floor V0=sup_strip Im M(x+i y_star) that governs the imp-2520 shock collision time t_c~1/(2 V0). FINDINGS: (F1) the 1/log gamma_N SHAPE IS reproduced -- the measured V0 is exactly linear in log(gamma/2pi) (invariant V0/log(gamma/2pi)=0.48458 constant to spread 3.3e-16 across the 5-rung ladder), so t_c~1/(2 V0) is exactly inverse-log, NOT a 1/log^2 nearest-pair d^2 law, and the Lemma B Gronwall floor exp(-2s/y^2) is respected along the flow (worst grid-sup/(sup0*floor)=0.991>0.98 at every rung); (F2) but the DIRECT anchor-to-crossover shrink is r_direct=V0(N*)/V0(N_x)=0.3870, NOT the assumed 0.4410 -- the whole gap is the 2pi inside the log: the flow shrinks as the LOCAL DENSITY log(gamma/2pi) (7.3602/19.0197=0.3870) whereas imp-398 used the BARE height log gamma_N (9.1981/20.8576=0.4410), so the closed form OVER-states the surviving crossover collision time by ~13.96%; (F3) re-anchoring the direct shape to the same A1-trap 2.37e-4 gives t_c(N_x)=9.1714e-5 (vs imp-3620 1.0452e-4) and the C_G=1 flow factor 1.0000917 (vs 1.0001045), STILL deep inside the imp-3604 bracket [1,1.000474] at ~19.3% of it and moving TOWARD 1, so the imp-3620 N_half/N_x band ~0.996 is unchanged at its published 6-digit precision. The seed is mesoscopic so only the density-floor SHOCK shape/ratio is measured, NOT the microscopic nearest-pair collision; the absolute shock constant c_sh (imp-2520 SG1, OPEN) is untouched and the scale is still pinned to 2.37e-4 exactly as imp-398 does. 6 self-computing assertions pass on import; import-light (effectiveHeightForN only, no heavy bundle). MEASUREMENT/DERIVATION only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3617, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:37:27Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3648 (numerical): extend the imp-3624 a-window sensitivity test of the fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) from n=3..6 to the imp-3618 deeper rungs n=7,8, reusing the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson moments M_0..M_16 (no new moment computation)", files: ["src/data/imp-3648-fit-bias-a-window-sensitivity-n78.js", "scripts/run-assertions.mjs"], detail: "imp-3624 certified the a-window robustness of the imp-3581/imp-3600 fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) (the fitted exponent moves as the a-grid moves, but the whole drift is captured by cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) against a window-INVARIANT D_n) only for n=3..6; imp-3618 extended the closed C_n/D_n ladder to n=7,8 (D_7~-1.5787e-4, D_8~-1.3198e-4) but only on the single fixed nine-rung (odd)/six-rung (even) ladder per parity. This module runs the SAME six imp-3624 windows (base/deep/shallow/coarse/dense/short6; covVar ~0.00286..0.05957, a ~20x range) for n=7,8, reusing the SAME MOMENTS[0..16] on the NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson grid (which already carry the M_11..M_14 imp-3618 feeds the deep ladder) -- NO new moment computation. RESULT: across all 12 (n in {7,8}, six-window) cells the fitted least-squares exponent MOVES by up to 8.95e-6 (n=7) between windows while the residual slopeModelErr=|p_fit-fitted| stays at the imp-3624 ~1e-9 level (global max 8.32e-10), four orders below the drift it explains; the extracted (fitted-2)/covVar recovers the closed D_7~-1.5787e-4 / D_8~-1.3198e-4 to <=9.58e-5 relative at every window, so D_n is window-invariant and the read-out drift IS exactly the cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) term at the deeper rungs too, not an unmodeled effect. Two independent cross-checks vs imp-3618 pin the module to the certified ladder: the n=7 base window (nine odd rungs) reproduces the imp-3618 fitted 1.99999536, the n=8 short6 window (six even rungs) reproduces 1.99999214. So the tail exponent is EXACTLY 2 window by window at n=7,8 and the sub-2 read-out is the derived O(a^2) curvature bias, extending the imp-3624 n=3..6 result up the certified imp-3618 ladder. 9 self-computing assertions pass on import (import-light, no heavy assembly); build passes. MEASUREMENT only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3618, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:38:18Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3647 (numerical): extend the imp-3622 planted-feature (xi_true=250) argmax test to the sub-floor regime N in {400,512,640,700,764,900} BELOW the imp-3582 replica-hiding floor, measuring the in-band aliasing leakage margin -- the generic N_replica~764 is a WORST-CASE bound; the mid-band feature has its own LOWER fold-in floor N_fold~620.70, and the drift-0 discriminator fails exactly at/below it (two equal comb peaks) and holds strictly above", files: ["src/data/imp-3647-below-floor-replica-foldin-margin.js"], detail: "imp-3622 confirmed the 2 m xi_Nyq per-doubling replica drift for a planted cosine at xi_true=250 at the four imp-3558 rungs N in {1200,2400,4800,9600}, all ABOVE the imp-3582 floor N_replica=xi_max U/pi=2400/pi~764, but never tested the sub-floor regime where a first-order replica L=2 xi_Nyq-xi_true folds into (0,400]. This module MEASURES the periodogram at N in {400,512,640,700,764,900} with the SAME planted feature. KEY HONEST FINDING: the generic 764 is a WORST-CASE bound (loosest in-band source xi_true=xi_max=400, replica folds in as soon as xi_Nyq<=xi_max); a specific mid-band source at 250 has its OWN, LOWER fold-in floor N_fold=(xi_max+xi_true)U/(2pi)=1950/pi~620.70, strictly BELOW 764. The measured ladder splits exactly there: N in {900,764,700,640} (all >620.70) keep the replica at 692.48/550.06/483.04/420.21 above the band ceiling 400, so (0,400] holds ONE peak (genuine at 250), argmax pinned, drift-0 DECISIVE -- and this holds even for N=764,700,640 which lie BELOW the generic 764; N in {512,400} (both <620.70) fold the replica IN at 286.17/168.88 with periodogram height EXACTLY equal to the genuine peak (Dirichlet comb, rel diff ~1e-15 measured), so (0,400] holds TWO equal maxima and drift-0 is NO LONGER decisive. The replica sweeps THROUGH the genuine peak at N_colocate=xi_true U/pi=1500/pi~477.46 (between 512 and 400), the worst masking case. CAVEAT: a coarse in-band scan on the imp-3558 step dxi=0.1 keeps 250 an on-grid node while the folded replica is off-node, so the coarse argmax reports 250 at EVERY rung even where the equal-height replica is in-band -- the grid artifact that makes a naive coarse drift-0 read unsafe below the floor; the decisive quantity is the in-band comb-peak count, not the coarse argmax. So the imp-3582 764 correctly UPPER-bounds the replica-free grid size across all in-band sources but is not the failure point for any single feature. 10 self-computing assertions pass on import; import-light (no heavy bundle). MEASUREMENT/certification only on a SYNTHETIC test signal (not the |P1| objective); gives xi* no closed form (imp-3470 stationarity stays transcendental); RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3619, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:39:30Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3606 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3576 inner-A(tau) composite-Simpson truncation constant K_n^inner \u2013\u2013 clean O(h^4), monotone-decreasing ~4x/rung, curvature at the tau~0 overlap peak, falsifying the imp-3547 tail-redistribution hypothesis", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3547 flagged the inner-fraction ladder over M_0..M_3 (0.911/0.963/0.903/0.955) as non-monotone without deriving the underlying inner-truncation constant. imp-3576 isolated K_n^inner via a Richardson inner-panel h-ladder and found it is clean O(h^4) (observed order to 4.000, stable to <0.3%) and STRICTLY MONOTONE DECREASING (6.88e-2, 2.45e-2, 5.51e-3, 1.28e-3, 3.14e-4 for M_0..M_4, ~4x per rung), with the error density C(tau) concentrated at the tau~0 overlap peak and dead by tau>=1 -- the opposite of the ticket hypothesis that tau^n redistributes mass toward a high-curvature tail, which is thereby falsified. Because innerFraction=1-|sInner-ref|/|sBase-ref| cancels the |M_n| normalization, the imp-3547 non-monotone parity alternation is carried entirely by the leftover outer-grid Simpson residual, decoupled from the monotone K_n^inner. Added a new glossary entry documenting this with the standard honest-scope banner (measurement/derivation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3620, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:40:36Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3646 (numerical): assess large-n asymptotics of the imp-3581/imp-3618 closed remainder-tail coefficients by measuring the driving moment ratio Q_n=M_(n+2)/M_n across n=3..18 -- REFUTES the fixed A-scale b^2 saturation guess: Q_n diverges slowly via a Laplace saddle, so C_n~(ln n)^2/(16 n^2) and D_n,|p_fit-2|->0 as O((ln n)^2/n^3) with NO finite-constant limit", files: ["src/data/imp-3646-remainder-tail-moment-ratio-asymptotics.js"], detail: "imp-3600/imp-3618/imp-3638 certified the closed C_n=M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n), D_n=C_(n+2)-C_n and the p=2 fit-bias law rung-by-rung through n=9,10 but never characterized the large-n behaviour of the driving moment ratio Q_n=M_(n+2)/M_n. This module MEASURES Q_n across n=3..18 on the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson reference. KEY NEGATIVE/CORRECTIVE FINDING: the natural fixed-A-scale guess (Q_n -> b^2, giving C_n~b^2/n^2 with a constant prefactor) is REFUTED. The A-weight A(tau)=int Phi(s)Phi(s+tau)ds decays SUPER-exponentially (A(0.5)~4.5e-11, A(1)~3e-75, A(tau)~exp(-pi e^{4tau})) with NO hard support endpoint on [0,T_A], so Q_n GROWS slowly and without bound (Q_3~0.02915, Q_6~0.05216, Q_10~0.08020, Q_14~0.10545, Q_18~0.12840) and n^2 C_n is STRICTLY INCREASING over n=3..18 (0.0131->0.1095): C_n is NOT a fixed b^2/n^2. The growth is governed by the Laplace saddle of the moment integrand tau^n A(tau): the peak sits at tau*(n) solving n=4 pi tau* e^{4tau*} (log-derivative of tau^n exp(-pi e^{4tau})), and the measured Q_n/tau*^2 falls monotonically to 1 from above (1.207 at n=6 -> 1.099 at n=10 -> 1.040 at n=18 -> 1.034 at n=20), confirming Q_n~tau*(n)^2 with tau*(n)~(ln n)/4. Hence the closed slowly-varying decay laws C_n=Q_n/((n+1)(n+2))~(ln n)^2/(16 n^2) (O((ln n)^2/n^2), log-divergent n^2 C_n prefactor), D_n=C_(n+2)-C_n<0 -> 0 like O((ln n)^2/n^3), and |p_fit-2|=|D_n|cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) -> 0 like O((ln n)^2/n^3): a genuine DECAY law (all three -> 0) but NO finite-constant n->inf limit for Q_n or n^2 C_n. This explains and is consistent with the imp-3618/imp-3638 monotone same-parity |p_fit-2| decrease (|D_n| shrinks with a log-varying prefactor, not a pure n^-3). 8 self-computing assertions pass on import (moment ratio grows, n^2 C_n grows, saddle ratio -> 1, D_n<0, |D_n| shrinks, C_n=Q_n/((n+1)(n+2)) exact, verdict, honesty); build passes. MEASUREMENT/DERIVATION only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator-level K_a>=0 positivity (imp-3066) UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3621, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:43:48Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3607 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3579 miss-factor moment-cancellation –– the derived degree-d bridge miss factor 1 - 1/k^(d+1) is moment-independent (a^d homogeneity cancels M_d in the scaling ratio) so the imp-3557 moment refinement shifts it EXACTLY zero", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3579 propagated the imp-3557 refined moments (M_4=9.62528e-8, M_3, relative corrections ~1.55e-6 to ~5.41e-6 across M_2..M_5) into the imp-3488 degree-2 (1-1/k^3) and imp-3510 degree-3 (1-1/k^4) bridge-mass miss-factor constants. Because the moment M_d is the leading coefficient in (a^d/d!)M_d and cancels identically in the scaling ratio r_k=B_d(a/k)/B_d(a)=k^{-d}, the derived closed-form constants carry no moment and shift by EXACTLY zero under the refinement; the only residual sensitivity is through the O(a^2) tail via the moment ratio M_(d+2)/M_d, where a two-term model shows the miss factor shifts by only ~1e-10 -- four-plus orders below the propagated moment correction and ~seven orders inside the leading-form tail budget. Added a new glossary entry documenting this moment-cancellation fact with the standard honest-scope banner (measurement/certification only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3622, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:48:27Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3608 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3580 sigma=1/2 <=> E_coll=E_trunc crossover coincidence being EXACTLY floor-invariant while the ~0.40% flow-gap grows monotonically 0.228%->0.687% across the half-to-double E_trunc floor grid", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3556 certified at a single baseline E_trunc floor that the sigma(N)=1/2 half-decay coincides with the imp-3444 E_coll=E_trunc crossover. imp-3580 re-root-solved both crossings across the imp-3443 half-to-double E_trunc floor grid (0.5x..2x) and found: (1) the coincidence itself is EXACTLY floor-invariant -- x(N_x)=E_coll/E_trunc=1.000000 at every node, a structural odds-ratio property (sigma=x/(1+x) so sigma=1/2 iff x=1), not a baseline accident; (2) the N_half/N_x ratio stays in a tight band [0.99313,0.99772]~0.996 across the grid, reproducing imp-3556 exactly at the baseline node; (3) but the ~0.40% flow-gap is NOT a fixed constant -- it grows monotonically 0.228% (0.5x floor) to 0.687% (2x floor), tracking the structural law gap~2 E_flow(N_x)/E_trunc within ~5%, correcting a literal gap-stays-constant reading. Added a new glossary entry documenting this with the standard honest-scope banner (measurement/certification only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3623, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:54:15Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3609 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3581 analytic derivation of the moment-remainder tail exponent p=2 -- the closed leading coefficient C_n=M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n) and the fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) that explains why the imp-3553 nine-rung fit reads 1.99999 (|p-2|~1.2e-5), not exactly 2", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3502/imp-3553 FIT the same-parity moment-remainder tail exponent to p~2 (imp-3553 to 1.99999 on a nine-rung cancellation-free ladder) but neither DERIVED p=2 nor explained the ~1.2e-5 shortfall. imp-3581 derives it: peeling the leading term of R_n(a)=sum_{m>=n,step2} a^m/m! M_m gives the relative residual r_n(a)=C_n a^2[1+D_n a^2+O(a^4)] with the CLOSED leading coefficient C_n=M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n) (reducing to C_3=M_5/(20 M_3), C_4=M_6/(30 M_4)), so the leading power of a is EXACTLY 2 -- the exponent is derived, not fitted. The next-order coefficient D_n gives the closed fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a), which MEASURED reproduces the actual least-squares slope to ~1e-9 on both the odd and even ladders, certifying the imp-3553 1.99999 equals the derived 2 up to a fully-quantified O(a^2) curvature bias, not exponent drift. Added a new glossary entry documenting this with the standard honest-scope banner (measurement/derivation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3624, timestamp: "2026-07-03T13:58:38Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3610 (content): add a glossary entry for the imp-3582 analytic replica-hiding grid threshold N_replica = xi_max U/pi ~ 764 -- the grid size below which a first-order midpoint-quadrature aliasing replica 2 xi_Nyq - xi_true can fold into the (0,400] scan band, hardening the imp-3558 argmax-drift-0 discriminator with an analytic floor (all four ladder rungs sit ~1.57x above it)", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3558 rested its far-tail argmax-drift-0 discriminator on an EMPIRICAL contrast (a folded-in replica would move ~8797 across the ladder while genuine peaks stay fixed) without deriving the grid size below which a replica could still hide. imp-3582 supplies that floor: midpoint quadrature on [0,U] samples at frequency 2 xi_Nyq, so a genuine feature aliases to L=2 xi_Nyq-xi_true, and the whole scanned band (0,400] is replica-free iff xi_Nyq<=xi_max, i.e. N > N_replica = xi_max U/pi ~ 763.94 (ceil 764). The smallest imp-3558 rung N=1200 clears this by a factor ~1.57, so all four rungs are analytically replica-free, not just empirically distinct. Added a new glossary entry documenting N_replica, the tighter co-location floor (~688) and main-maximizer floor (~394), with the standard honest-scope banner (derivation/certification only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3625, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:05:08Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3611 (ux): add a viz page for the imp-3575 corrected-Krylov skew-Toeplitz gap ladder", files: ["src/data/imp-3611-skew-toeplitz-krylov-gap-ladder-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3611SkewToeplitzKrylovGapLadderViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3575 traced the imp-3555 non-monotone N=1600 skew-Toeplitz gap rung to a Lanczos Krylov-truncation deficit in lambda_3 (the m=200 reference rho=0.9993548 was still climbing; it locks at 0.99975799 by m=240) and showed the corrected -log rho(N) ladder is strictly decreasing through N=2000 with local slopes -1.9933/-1.9949 continuing toward the -2 section-gap heuristic, but that measurement had no page consumer. Added a new lightweight viz-data module (baked reference literals reproduced from the imp-3575 measured.krylovSweep/correctedLadder fields and the imp-3555 non-monotone bake, no heavy Lanczos re-run on import) and a page rendering two SVG charts: the N=1600 rho(m) Krylov-depth sweep (artifact rung at m=200 vs the converged lock, contrasted with the already-converged N=1200 anchor), and the restored -log rho(N) ladder across N={800,1000,1200,1600,2000} with the imp-3555 artifact rung shown alongside the corrected one to make the monotonicity restoration visible. Wired the route /viz-imp3611-skew-toeplitz-krylov-gap-ladder into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3540/3563/3586/3589 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3626, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:11:02Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3612 (ux): add a viz page for the imp-3581 remainder-tail fit-bias depth sweep, marking the imp-3553 nine-rung point and the p_fit=2+D_n cov/var predicted curve", files: ["src/data/imp-3612-fit-bias-depth-sweep-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3612FitBiasDepthSweepViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3581 derived the moment-remainder tail exponent p=2 in closed form and showed the least-squares fitted slope falls short of 2 by an O(a^2) log-log curvature bias, p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a), that shrinks monotonically as the odd R_3 ladder deepens (|p_fit-2| from 6.66e-5 at 3 rungs to 3.19e-6 at 18 rungs), with the imp-3553 nine-rung cancellation-free fit (1.16e-5) sitting exactly on that curve -- but that measurement had no page consumer. Added a new lightweight viz-data module (baked reference literals reproduced from the imp-3581 measured.depthSweep/oddCase.nextOrderCoeff fields, plus the predicted-curve values computed from the same closed p_fit formula, no heavy Phi-kernel/Simpson-quadrature re-run on import) and a page rendering an SVG chart of |p_fit-2| vs ladder depth on a log scale: the actual least-squares deviation, the closed-form predicted curve overlaid (matching to <1e-4 relative at every depth), and the imp-3553 nine-rung point marked distinctly. Wired the route /viz-imp3612-fit-bias-depth-sweep into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3540/3563/3586/3589/3611 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3627, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:18:15Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3613 (ux): add a viz page for the imp-3582 aliasing fold-in geometry, showing the three fold-in floors (N=394/688/764) and the four imp-3558 rungs sitting replica-free above all of them", files: ["src/data/imp-3613-replica-fold-in-geometry-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3613ReplicaFoldInGeometryViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3582 derived the analytic replica-hiding grid threshold N_replica=xi_max U/pi~764 (plus the tighter N_colocate~688 and N-star~394 refinements) hardening the imp-3558 argmax-drift-0 discriminator, but the derivation had no page consumer. Added a lightweight viz-data module (baked literals recomputed from the imp-3582 VERBATIM xiNyqOf/replicaLoc formulas, no heavy import) and a page rendering two SVG charts: a zoomed linear view of the three replica-location lines L(xi_true,N)=2 xi_Nyq-xi_true crossing the (0,400] band ceiling at N=394/688/764, and a wide log-N view extending the band-top line out to the imp-3558 ladder N={1200,2400,4800,9600}, each rung plotted well above the ceiling to show the band is replica-free at every rung. Wired the route /viz-imp3613-replica-fold-in-geometry into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3540/3563/3586/3589/3611/3612 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3628, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:33:02Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3614 (ux): add a viz page for the imp-3580 sigma-crossover floor invariance, plotting the N_half/N_x ratio band and the measured-vs-structural-law flow gap across the half-to-double E_trunc floor grid", files: ["src/data/imp-3614-sigma-crossover-floor-invariance-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3614SigmaCrossoverFloorInvarianceViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "imp-3580 re-root-solved the sigma=1/2 half-decay crossing N_half and the E_coll=E_trunc crossover N_x across the imp-3443 half-to-double E_trunc floor grid f in {0.5,0.75,1.0,1.5,2.0}, certifying the N_half/N_x ratio stays in the tight band [0.99313,0.99772]~0.996 while the flow gap 1-N_half/N_x grows monotonically 0.228%->0.687%, tracking the structural law 2 E_flow(N_x)/E_trunc -- but the result had no page consumer. Added a lightweight viz-data module (baked reference literals taken from the imp-3580 floorGrid, no heavy import) and a page rendering two SVG charts: the N_half/N_x ratio vs floor factor with the band shaded and the baseline f=1.0x node (reproducing imp-3556) marked, and the measured flow-gap vs the structural-law prediction showing the honest refinement that the gap is not a fixed 0.40% constant. Wired the route /viz-imp3614-sigma-crossover-floor-invariance into App.jsx and added it to the documented EXEMPT_FROM_INDEX drift backlog in scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs (consistent with sibling imp-3611/3612/3613 viz tickets), so the nav-link audit still passes. Presentation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3629, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:41:00Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3615 (meta): audit whether the imp-3575/3576/3579/3580/3581/3582 research modules are imported by any page/component or are orphaned data files", files: ["src/data/imp-3615-3575-3582-cohort-module-surfacing-audit.js"], detail: "Continuing the imp-3459/3480/3498/3517/3539/3568/3593 orphan-audit series (which stopped at imp-3558) to the imp-3575..3582 cohort. Transitive import-graph walk from src/pages and src/components over real relative-import edges (string/comment mentions do not count) finds all six modules ORPHAN: imp-3575/3580/3581/3582 already have a routed viz page from the imp-3611/3614/3612/3613 follow-up tickets, but each viz-data consumer bakes its own reference literals with zero import statements rather than importing the source module, so the source file itself stays off the import graph; imp-3576 and imp-3579 have only a glossary.js prose mention (also not an import edge). Recorded the finding as a read-only audit module with self-checking assertions; no new bound, no QED, Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. No pages fabricated.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3630, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:02:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3661 (numerical): propagate the imp-3642 density correction (log(gamma/2pi) vs bare log gamma_N) into the imp-3620 closed-form t_c(N_x) pin and imp-3604 flow-factor bracket occupancy", files: ["src/data/imp-3661-sigma-crossover-tc-density-corrected-pin.js"], detail: "imp-3642 direct RK4 attractive-Dyson flow found the imp-398/imp-3620 closed-form collision time uses the BARE height log gamma_N, whereas the actual mesoscopic shock time scales with the LOCAL density log(gamma/2pi), so the crossover shrink is 0.3870 not 0.4410 and the bare-log pin over-states t_c(N_x) by ~13.96%. This module re-derives the imp-3620 t_c(N) closed form with the density-corrected log(gamma/2pi) argument and re-root-solves both crossings on the imp-3443 floor grid: (F1) the crossover-scale flow factor is pinned to 1.0000917 at C_G=1 (vs imp-3620 1.0001045), at ~19.3% of the imp-3604 bracket [1,1.000474] vs 22.05% -- the pin moves TOWARD 1; (F2) the imp-3620 N_half/N_x ~0.996 band is UNCHANGED at published 6-digit precision (max ratio shift ~9e-8 across the grid, f=1 still 0.996019 at N_x=3.280294e9); (F3) the bare-log pin over-states by ~13.96% at f=1 (13.18%-14.64% across floors). Measurement/derivation only; no positivity, NO QED; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3631, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:35:06Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3664 (numerical): extend the imp-3646 moment-ratio saddle law to n=40 and fit the sub-leading saddle correction of tau*(n)", files: ["src/data/imp-3664-moment-ratio-saddle-law-n40-extension.js"], detail: "imp-3646 measured Q_n=M_(n+2)/M_n across n=3..18 and derived it is governed by the Laplace saddle tau*(n) solving n=4 pi tau* e^{4 tau*} with Q_n/tau*^2->1 from above, but only to n=20 and with the sub-leading correction unfit. This module extends the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson moment ladder (M_0..M_42) and the bisection saddle solve to n=40: (1) the residual rho_n=Q_n/tau*(n)^2-1 stays positive and falls MONOTONICALLY with no reversal (rho_20~3.389e-2, rho_30~1.703e-2, rho_40~1.005e-2), confirming Q_n/tau*^2->1 out to n=40 consistent with the derived slowly-varying law; (2) logs of the saddle equation give the closed expansion 4 tau*(n)=ln n - ln ln n - ln pi + (ln ln n + ln pi)/ln n + O(./ln^2 n), so tau*(n)=(1/4)[ln n - ln ln n - ln pi + (ln ln n + ln pi)/ln n + ...] and the sub-leading (ln ln n)/(ln n) coefficient is EXACTLY 1 in 4 tau*, confirmed against the numeric root to 0.22% at n=40 ([4 tau*-(ln n-ln ln n-ln pi)]*ln n=2.4445 vs ln ln 40+ln pi=2.4501, normalized ratio ~0.9978); the isolated two-parameter (l/L vs 1/L) split is near-collinear/ill-conditioned over n<=40 so the bundled correction is reported. Measurement/derivation only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3632, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:40:00Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3616 (bug): audit the imp-3575/3576/3579/3580/3581/3582 modules (and their four page consumers) for inadvertent false-QED or RH-overclaim framing", files: ["src/data/imp-3616-3575-3582-cohort-honesty-audit.js"], detail: "Per the imp-3594/imp-3499/imp-3480 honesty-audit pattern, re-read the verdict/scope/caveat blocks of imp-3575/3576/3579/3580/3581/3582 and their four known page consumers (Imp3611SkewToeplitzKrylovGapLadderViz.jsx, Imp3612FitBiasDepthSweepViz.jsx, Imp3613ReplicaFoldInGeometryViz.jsx, Imp3614SigmaCrossoverFloorInvarianceViz.jsx). All ten already state measurement/derivation-only, carry the RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient framing, note the imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel K_a>=0 obstruction is untouched, and cite Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 as the rigorous SOTA with no QED -- NO DRIFT found. Read-only audit; no repair needed. RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; Lambda<=0.2 SOTA. NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3633, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:36:34Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3662 (numerical): measure the seed-sensitivity of the imp-3642 mesoscopic invariant V0/log(gamma/2pi)=0.48458 to block size M, strip height y_star and perturbation amplitude", files: ["src/data/imp-3662-mesoscopic-invariant-seed-sensitivity.js"], detail: "Swept the imp-3642 attractive Calogero-Moser Step-2 backward-Dyson seed over M in {81,161,321}, y_star in {2d,4d,8d}, amp in {0.5x,1x,2x} (27 configs). FINDINGS: (F1) the gamma-independence is ROBUST -- the invariant V0/log(gamma/2pi) stays flat across the height ladder to ~9.4e-16 at every seed, so V0 is genuinely linear in log(gamma/2pi) at any fixed seed; (F2) but the VALUE 0.48458 is seed/quadrature-dependent, ranging [0.43792,0.50627] (spread 6.84e-2, ~14%) dominated by two comparable finite-block-truncation levers, strip height y_star (marginally largest) and block size M, converging toward the ~0.5=(1/2)coth(pi*y_star/d) continuum floor, with perturbation amplitude far weakest; imp-3642 0.48458 (M=161,y_star=4d) sits ~3% below the ~0.5 continuum value; (F3) the Gronwall floor exp(-2s/y_star^2) is respected (>0.98, worst 0.9908) at amp<=1x for all M/y_star but VIOLATED at double amplitude (worst 0.9342, M=81/y_star=8d), so Lemma B is robust at the baseline seed but not amplitude-independent. Named residual sg-3662-continuum-floor-extrapolation. Measurement/derivation only; no positivity, NO QED; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3634, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:40:15Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3665 (numerical): independently cross-check the imp-3646 super-exponential A-weight decay claim A(tau)=int Phi(s)Phi(s+tau) ds ~ exp(-pi e^{4tau}) at tau in {0.5,1,1.5,2} via a LOG-DOMAIN recompute -- CONFIRMS the leading law and its slope, corrects the quoted A(1) 3e-75 -> 2.1e-75", files: ["src/data/imp-3665-a-weight-superexp-decay-crosscheck.js"], detail: "imp-3646 refuted the Q_n=M_(n+2)/M_n saturation guess resting on the assertion that A(tau) decays super-exponentially with no hard support endpoint (A(0.5)~4.5e-11, A(1)~3e-75, A(tau)~exp(-pi e^{4tau})); those magnitudes and the exponential law were never independently checked. Because A(1.5)~e^{-1267}~1e-550 and A(2)~e^{-9363}~1e-4067 UNDERFLOW IEEE-754 double (the naive integrand Phi(s)Phi(s+tau) is exactly 0.0, so direct Simpson returns 0 and -ln A=inf), A(tau) is recomputed in the LOG DOMAIN: ln Phi via log-sum-exp over the NPHI kernel terms (ln|amp_n|-pi n^2 e^{4u}, all positive for u>=0) and the composite Simpson as a log-sum-exp of ln(w)+lnPhi(s)+lnPhi(s+tau)+ln(h/3), giving -ln A exactly at all four tau. FINDINGS: (1) the leading law is CONFIRMED -- -ln A(tau)/(pi e^{4tau}) -> 1 from above (1.0266, 1.0025, 0.99987, 0.99977); (2) the central-difference slope d(-lnA)/dtau matches 4 pi e^{4tau} to <1% at every rung, ratio -> 1 (0.9925, 0.9997, 0.9993, 0.9999); (3) NO hard support endpoint -- extending the outer cutoff [0,7]->[0,12] refines -ln A by only ~1e-3 relative and never truncates, confirming the no-hard-endpoint premise behind imp-3646 C_n~(ln n)^2/(16 n^2); (4) A(0.5)~4.47e-11 matches the quoted 4.5e-11 to two figures. ONE honest correction: the converged A(1)~2.1e-75 (-ln A~171.955), not the 3e-75 imp-3646 quoted from its coarser n=1200 [0,7] Simpson (which under-resolves the sharp near-s=0 peak and gives -ln A~171.6); SAME order, leading law intact, a ~30% amplitude refinement not a regime change. 8 self-computing assertions pass on import; build passes. MEASUREMENT/CROSS-CHECK only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator-level K_a>=0 positivity (imp-3066) UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3635, timestamp: "2026-07-03T16:12:00Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3663 (numerical): close the named sub-gap sg-3645-matched-pair-depth-sweep -- measure minimal converged Krylov depth m*(N) for the FIXED lambda_5=lambda_6 pair across N in {1600,2000,2400} to discriminate the depth law", files: ["src/data/imp-3663-matched-pair-krylov-depth-sweep.js", "scripts/compute-imp3663-matched-pair-depth-sweep.mjs"], detail: "imp-3645 left m*(N) UNDER-DETERMINED because its two anchors were at different pair indices (N=1600 lambda_3 pair2 m*=280; N=2000 lambda_5=lambda_6 pair3 m*=480). Re-ran the identical imp-3505/imp-3575/imp-3625 skew-Toeplitz Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10,H0=0.025,midpoint) single full-reorthogonalization Lanczos at N in {1600,2000,2400} for the FIXED lambda_5=lambda_6 third pair, reading top-6 Gram Ritz at a 40-step sub-depth grid. RESULTS: (1) the matched-pair anchor TRIPLE is m*(1600)=360, m*(2000)=480, m*(2400)=560 (N=2000 reproduces the imp-3625 anchor EXACTLY -- m=440 pair56=1.010245749617736e-11 to full precision); (2) the fixed-pair m* GENUINELY GROWS with N, CORRECTING imp-3645 flat-in-N reading (a grid-floor artifact of the lambda_3 pair); (3) the growth is SUB-LINEAR/CONCAVE -- equal Delta N=400 gives decelerating Delta m 120->80 -- so LINEAR is disfavoured; least-squares RMS ranks log~4.7<sqrt~7.1<linear~9.4; (4) log vs sqrt NOT separated (RMS gap ~2.4 below the +/-20 grid quantisation) -- named residual sg-3663-log-vs-sqrt-fixed-pair; (5) matched m*(2400)=560 UNDERCUTS imp-3645 bracket 644..680 and the matched fits extrapolate N=3200 to ~706..767 vs imp-3645 linear 1080 (imp-3645 over-estimated by ~15%..40% via a pair-index-confounded slope 0.5; matched slope ~0.25). Measurement/fit only, self-computing, import-light; no positivity, NO QED; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; RH-EQUIVALENT; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3636, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:43:49Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3636 (meta): audit whether the imp-3599/3600/3601/3602/3603/3604 research modules are imported by any page/component consumer or are orphaned data files", files: ["src/data/imp-3636-3599-3604-cohort-module-surfacing-audit.js"], detail: "Continuing the imp-3459/3480/3498/3517/3539/3568/3593/3615 orphan-audit series (which stopped at imp-3582) to the imp-3599..3604 cohort. Transitive import-graph walk from src/pages and src/components over real relative-import edges (glossary/comment mentions and downstream-research-module imports that are themselves unreached do not count) finds all six modules ORPHAN. Unlike the imp-3615 cohort (four of six already had a routed viz page), NONE of these six has any page, component, or glossary.js entry yet: imp-3599/3600/3601/3602/3604 each already have a queued glossary ticket and viz ticket (imp-3626..3635) awaiting processing, so no new surfacing ticket is needed for them; imp-3603 (inner-truncation Gauss-Legendre cross-validation) has no queued surfacing ticket and is a cross-check utility feeding downstream verification modules (imp-3621, imp-3644) rather than a standalone narrative result, so it is recommended to stay an intentionally-unwired compute module, consistent with the imp-3576/imp-3579 precedent. Recorded as a read-only audit module with self-checking assertions; no new bound, no QED, Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. No pages fabricated.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3637, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:42:03Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3667 (numerical): extend the imp-3648 a-window sensitivity test of the fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) from n=7,8 to the imp-3638-certified rungs n=9,10", files: ["src/data/imp-3667-fit-bias-a-window-sensitivity-n910.js"], detail: "imp-3648 certified the a-window robustness of the imp-3581/imp-3600 fit-bias law at the deep rungs n=7,8; imp-3638 extended the certified C_n/D_n ladder to n=9,10 but only on the single fixed nine-rung (odd)/six-rung (even) ladder per parity. This module runs the SAME six imp-3624 windows (covVar factor ~0.00286 to ~0.05957, a ~20x range) for n=9 (odd, C_9=M_11/(110 M_9)~6.67939e-4, D_9~-1.1181e-4) and n=10 (even, C_10=M_12/(132 M_10)~6.07591e-4, D_10~-9.582e-5), reusing the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson moments extended to M_18. FINDINGS: across all 12 (n in {9,10}, six-window) cells the fitted least-squares exponent MOVES by up to 6.34e-6 (n=9) between windows while the residual slopeModelErr=|p_fit-fitted| stays at the imp-3648 ~1e-9 level (global max 5.33e-10), and (fitted-2)/covVar recovers the closed D_9/D_10 to <=8.66e-5 relative at every window, so D_n is window-invariant and the read-out drift IS the cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) term at these rungs too. Two cross-checks vs imp-3638 baked fitted exponents pin the module to the certified ladder: the n=9 base window reproduces the nine-rung 1.99999671, the n=10 short6 window the six-rung 1.99999429. So the tail exponent is EXACTLY 2 window by window at n=9,10 and the sub-2 read-out is the derived O(a^2) curvature bias. 9 self-computing assertions pass on import; build passes. MEASUREMENT only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator-level K_a>=0 positivity (imp-3066) UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3638, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:45:27Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3668 (numerical): dense-certify the FIFTH skew-Toeplitz pair lambda_9=lambda_10 at the deep rungs N in {1200,1600,2000} with the imp-3623/imp-3643 independent full-spectrum solver (Householder tred1 + implicit-QL tql1, no Krylov), one pair beyond imp-3643 -- the dense lambda_9=lambda_10 spread is 0 at N=1200/1600 and 1.38e-15 at N=2000 (< 1.4e-15 everywhere), so the deep section spectrum is FIVE-pair adjacent-paired; the fifth-pair amplitude sigma_4=lambda_9/lambda_1 climbs 0.99657->0.99807->0.99876 toward 1 with depth; dense top-8 reproduce the imp-3643 baked top-8 to all printed digits", files: ["src/data/imp-3668-skew-toeplitz-fifth-pair-dense-crossval.js", "scripts/imp-3668-dense-fifth-pair-offline.mjs"], detail: "Extends the imp-3643 dense fourth-pair certification (lambda_7=lambda_8) by one spectrum level, extracting the TOP-TEN Gram eigenvalues of S=T^T T from the identical imp-3505 assembly (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) via the same non-Lanczos dense route. Certifies the lambda_9=lambda_10 adjacent-pairing degeneracy at machine precision and reports the pairing-certified sigma_4 amplitude the pending distinct Lanczos amplitude-law ticket will read. Pairing-structure cross-check only, does NOT establish the amplitude LAW, does NOT attempt imp-3066 K_a>=0; RH-equivalent, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3639, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:49:27Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3637 (bug): audit the imp-3599/3600/3601/3602/3603/3604 modules for inadvertent false-QED or RH-overclaim framing", files: ["src/data/imp-3637-3599-3604-cohort-honesty-audit.js"], detail: "Per the imp-3616/imp-3594/imp-3499 honesty-audit pattern, re-read the verdict/scope/honestCaveat blocks of imp-3599/3600/3601/3602/3603/3604. All six already state measurement/derivation-only, carry the RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient framing, note the imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel K_a>=0 obstruction is untouched, and cite Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 as the rigorous SOTA with no QED -- NO DRIFT found. Cross-checked against the imp-3636 orphan audit: none of the six has a page/component consumer, so there is no on-page copy to drift either. Read-only audit; no repair needed. RH-EQUIVALENT; imp-3066 UNTOUCHED; Lambda<=0.2 SOTA. NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3640, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:48:03Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3666 (numerical): map the imp-3647 feature-specific fold-in floor N_fold(xi_true)=(xi_max+xi_true)U/(2pi) across a ladder of planted xi_true in {100,150,200,250,300,350,400} and locate where it meets the generic imp-3582 764", files: ["src/data/imp-3666-feature-foldin-floor-ladder.js"], detail: "imp-3647 measured the feature-specific fold-in floor only for the single planted source xi_true=250 (N_fold~620.70 < generic 764). This module maps the whole line by direct planted-comb periodogram across xi_true in {100..400}: (1) N_fold(xi_true) is LINEAR -- OLS recovers slope U/(2pi)=3/pi~0.9549 to 1.1e-16 and intercept xi_max U/(2pi)=1200/pi~381.97 exactly, R^2=1, constant per-50-step increment 150/pi~47.75; N_fold = 477.46/525.21/572.96/620.70/668.45/716.20/763.94. (2) The TOP rung xi_true=xi_max=400 lands EXACTLY on the generic imp-3582 worst-case floor 2400/pi~763.94 (764 rounded), so the generic floor is the xi_true=xi_max ENDPOINT of the feature line, not a separate constant; the feature-floor gap below 764, (xi_max-xi_true)U/(2pi)=286.48/238.73/190.99/143.24/95.49/47.75/0.00, is itself linear and closes at the endpoint. (3) At each rung the straddling grids N_below=floor(N_fold)/N_above=floor+1 MEASURE the split -- replica image in-band below (2 in-band peaks) / out above (1) -- bracketing N_fold at every rung; mid-band folded replicas tie the genuine peak to rel.diff ~1e-15. (4) BONUS: the endpoint is a TRIPLE coincidence N_fold=N_colocate=2400/pi (solving (xi_max+xi_true)/2=xi_true gives xi_true=xi_max), the single point where the replica lands ON the genuine peak (total masking merge); every mid-band replica is separately resolvable below its floor. Measurement/certification only; RH-equivalent; imp-3066 K_a>=0 UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3641, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:48:53Z", category: "accuracy", summary: "imp-3669 (accuracy): independently reproduce and verify the imp-3643 baked deep-rung dense top-8 Gram eigenvalues at N in {1200,1600,2000} via a Sturm-bisection re-solve of the re-typed imp-3505 assembly (entirely different from the imp-3643 implicit-QL); all eight literals reproduce to worst relative 1.77e-15 and sigma_3 to worst 3.38e-14 (below 1e-13), so the baked literals are CONFIRMED, no transcription/drift", files: ["src/data/imp-3669-dense-third-gap-independent-verify.js", "scripts/imp-3669-dense-third-gap-independent-verify.mjs"], detail: "imp-3643 bakes its deep-rung dense top-8 Gram eigenvalues of S=T^T T as literals from a one-off offline EISPACK Householder+implicit-QL solve (scripts/imp-3643-dense-third-gap-offline.mjs). This ticket guards those literals against a transcription or offline-drift error by an INDEPENDENT re-solve: scripts/imp-3669-dense-third-gap-independent-verify.mjs re-types the imp-3505 Ttilde assembly (Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R, NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) from scratch, forms the Gram explicitly at N in {1200,1600,2000}, and extracts the top-8 by STURM-SEQUENCE BISECTION on the Householder tridiagonal -- a routine entirely different from the imp-3643 implicit-QL (tql1). RESULT: every rung reproduces all eight imp-3643 baked denseTop8 literals to a worst relative deviation of 1.77e-15 (machine precision), and the independent third gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 agrees with the imp-3619 baked Lanczos sigma_3Lan to worst 3.38e-14 at N=1600 (1.30e-14 at N=1200, 2.22e-16 at N=2000), below the imp-3643 XVAL_TOL=1e-13 and consistent with its <3.5e-14 claim. So the imp-3643 baked literals and their <1e-13 self-consistency are CONFIRMED before downstream tickets (imp-3668) build on them. Import-light data module with 5 self-checking assertions passing on import. Householder tridiagonalization is standard and shared with imp-3643 (a spectrum-preserving orthogonal similarity); the independence lever is the Sturm-bisection eigenvalue extraction plus the re-typed assembly. Verification/measurement only, imp-3066 K_a>=0 UNTOUCHED, NO QED, RH-equivalent, Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3642, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:52:00Z", category: "proof", summary: "imp-3671 (proof): assess whether the imp-3642 direct-flow mesoscopic density floor V0(gamma) supplies a quantitative Lipschitz modulus for the open Step-4 G6a_shock_lipschitz -- verdict STRUCTURALLY SILENT (type/dimension + Gronwall-vacuous scale)", files: ["src/data/imp-3671-mesoscopic-v0-vs-g6a-shock-lipschitz-assessment.js"], detail: "The roadmap names G6a_shock_lipschitz (the Hoelder-1/2 modulus C_Lip of the collision-time field tau_c(x) at the Burgers shock front, Polymath15 Lemma 5.2) as the open Step-4 bridge sub-gap. imp-3642 directly measured the mesoscopic density floor V0(gamma)=sup Im M(x+i y_star) at y_star=4d, found it exactly linear in the local density log(gamma/2pi) (invariant 0.48458) and respecting the Gronwall floor exp(-2s/y_star^2)~0.991. This module ASSESSES whether that reading supplies C_Lip. VERDICT: STRUCTURALLY SILENT, two independent obstructions. (S1) TYPE/DIMENSION: V0 is a strip-SUP density scalar governing WHEN the shock forms (t_c~1/(2V0)); C_Lip is the SPATIAL modulus governing HOW the front bends in x. The strip sup erases the microscopic x-gradient structure, so a single density-floor scalar carries no (x-x_prime) difference information and is the wrong TYPE of object for a Hoelder-1/2 modulus. (S2) SCALE: grounded in the imp-3642 measured floor, E_meso=-ln(0.991)=0.009041=2s/y_star^2, so at strip height y=y_star/k the same floor is floor_meso^{k^2}, collapsing 0.991->0.865 at the mean spacing d, crossing 1/2 at k~8.76 (~0.46d, above the true nearest-pair gap), reaching 1.5e-10 at ~0.08d -- the mesoscopic contraction is Gronwall-VACUOUS at the microscopic front, exactly imp-2520 negative-finding 1 that the nearest-pair regime is a different, Gronwall-vacuous scale. What V0 DOES supply is the collision-TIME scale, which per imp-2564 feeds the E(N) bridge CONSTANTS (imp-3661 already propagated the density-corrected flow factor 1.0000917), NOT the headline inequality and NOT C_Lip; G6a stays OPEN. 5 self-computing assertions pass on import; build passes. ASSESSMENT/DERIVATION only, no bridge closure; RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3643, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:52:11Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3670 (numerical): measure the observable fit-bias decay |p_fit-2| across n=3..18 (imp-3624/imp-3648 base a-window) against the imp-3646-derived (ln n)^2/n^3 rate", files: ["src/data/imp-3670-fit-bias-decay-rate-vs-lnsq.js"], detail: "imp-3646 derived D_n and hence |p_fit-2|=|D_n| cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) -> 0 like O((ln n)^2/n^3) from the Laplace saddle Q_n=M_(n+2)/M_n ~ tau*(n)^2 (tau*~(ln n)/4), but the propagation to the OBSERVABLE least-squares fit-bias was never measured across the ladder. Recomputed p_fit at n=3..18 on the imp-3624/imp-3648 base window (aHi=0.5, ratio=0.5, K=9; covVar=0.0293884) using the SAME NM=1600 [0,T_A] Simpson moments extended to M_26 (four-term same-parity tail per rung); cross-checks reproduce the imp-3648 baked n=7 slope 1.9999953601 and the imp-3667 baked n=9 slope 1.9999967140. THREE readings: (1) OBSERVABLE LAW CONFIRMED -- |p_fit-2| equals |D_n| covVar to <=1.10e-9 at every rung and decays monotone 1.1575e-5 (n=3) -> 1.0786e-6 (n=18), so the closed C_n/D_n log-divergent-prefactor laws DO reach the observable; (2) NAIVE (ln n)^2/n^3 RATIO DRIFTS -- |p_fit-2|/((ln n)^2/n^3) is strictly increasing 2.59e-4 -> 7.53e-4 (~2.9x, still climbing at n=18), so the fully-simplified asymptotic form is NOT reached at n<=18; (3) the drift is the crude tau*(n)~(ln n)/4 substitution, NOT an unmodeled term -- the ACTUAL Laplace saddle tau*(n)^2 is faithful, |D_n|/|D_n^saddle| falls monotone to 1 from above (3.644->1.095, mirroring imp-3646 Q_n/tau*^2->1), while pure 1/n^3 drifts ~20x (confirming a real log-growing prefactor). Named residual sg-3670-lnn-saddle-not-asymptotic-at-n18: the (ln n)/4 substitution is pre-asymptotic through n=18; a larger-n ladder (or the exact tau*(n)) is needed to see the (ln n)^2/n^3 ratio plateau. 10 self-computing assertions pass on import; build passes. MEASUREMENT only, RH-EQUIVALENT necessary-but-not-sufficient; operator-level K_a>=0 positivity (imp-3066) UNTOUCHED; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3644, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:54:06Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3649 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3617 self-consistent O(eps^3) flow-gap expansion", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3617 pushed the imp-3599 exact flow-gap identity gap = 1-(L_half/L_x)/(1+eta)^2 to a self-consistent closed expansion Du=ln(N_half/N_x)=d1 eps+d2 eps^2+d3 eps^3, giving the resummed leading coefficient d1=-2/(1-lambda), the second coefficient d2 (first using the slope-curvature s=d^2 lnL/d(lnN)^2 and the E_flow log-curvature nu), and a third coefficient d3 adding the log-N third derivative t. Added a glossary entry recording the closed-form coefficients and the measured geometric convergence across the imp-3443 floor grid: at f=0.5 the residual falls 4.49e-4 (imp-3599 crude model) -> 6.54e-5 (leading d1) -> 1.38e-7 (O(eps^2)) -> 3.13e-10 (O(eps^3)), a ~5-6 order drop toward the ~1e-13 exact-identity floor, with the honest sub-gap imp-3617-fourthorder-fd-floor noting the O(eps^3) truncation still falls short of that floor. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3645, timestamp: "2026-07-03T14:59:42Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3650 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3618 extension of the p=2 moment-remainder tail exponent ladder to rungs n=7,8", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3581 derived the closed p=2 moment-remainder tail exponent and fit-bias law p_fit=2+D_n cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a), and imp-3600 certified it at rungs n=5,6. imp-3618 extended the ladder to the next rungs n=7 (odd sinh R_7) and n=8 (even cosh R_8), giving the closed leading coefficients C_7=M_9/(72 M_7)~8.25809e-4 and C_8=M_10/(90 M_8)~7.39567e-4 and next-order D_7~-1.5787e-4, D_8~-1.3198e-4, with the predicted fit-bias reproducing the actual least-squares slope to ~1e-9 at both new rungs (|p_fit-2|~4.64e-6 and ~7.86e-6), on the monotone same-parity trend. Added a glossary entry recording the closed forms, the measured certification, and the honest RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient scope. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3646, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:04:27Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3651 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3619 THIRD skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1, also converging to -2 and corroborating the j^2-1 amplitude law through pair j=4", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3602 measured the SECOND skew-Toeplitz gap sigma_2=lambda_5/lambda_1, found it converges to the same -2 section-gap exponent as the first gap rho=lambda_3/lambda_1, and reported the near-constant ratio -log sigma_2/-log rho ~ 8/3, the signature of a common N^-2 law with pair-index amplitude a_j proportional to (j^2-1), tested through only a single ratio (a_3/a_2=8/3). imp-3619 measured the THIRD gap sigma_3=lambda_7/lambda_1 on the identical assembly across N=160..2000 and found it ALSO converges to -2 (global q_3=-1.9817 vs q_1=-1.9811, R^2=0.99999 both), and corroborated the j^2-1 amplitude law at pair j=4 via two independent ratios: -log sigma_3/-log rho -> 5.00008 = a_4/a_2, and -log sigma_3/-log sigma_2 -> 1.87502 = a_4/a_3 = 15/8; lambda_7=lambda_8 pairing holds to < 4e-14, confirming a genuine fourth-pair level. Added a glossary entry mirroring the imp-3555 (first-gap -2 convergence) entry, recording the third-gap convergence, the two-ratio amplitude corroboration, and the honest RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient scope (imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3647, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:08:32Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3652 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3620 closed-form pin of the sigma-crossover flow factor via the imp-398 t_c(N)~1/log gamma_N law", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3604 bounded the N_half/N_x crossover ratio under the WHOLE Gronwall flow-factor bracket [1,1.000474], leaving the band [0.99313,0.99772] a bracket rather than a pinned value. imp-3620 derived the flow factor at the crossover scale from the named imp-398 backward-flow-stability law t_c(N)~1/log gamma_N, giving the closed form t_c(N)=2.37e-4*log(gamma_{N*})/log(gamma_N) (N*=1e4); at the baseline crossover N_x=3.280294e9 this pins the flow factor to 1.0001045 (C_G=1), only 22.05% of the imp-3604 bracket and strictly below the imp-3580 frozen value 1.000237 (a ~2.27x over-statement by the frozen node). Re-root-solving both crossings with the closed form collapses the imp-3604 per-floor sub-bracket to a single pinned N_half/N_x value (band still [0.99313,0.99772]~0.996) with only ~2-8e-7 residual C_G spread vs the imp-3604 ~3e-6 flat-bracket spread. Added a glossary entry mirroring the imp-3620 module's finding set. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3648, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:14:02Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3653 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3621 OUTER composite-Simpson truncation certification of the higher moments M_5..M_10", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3600 fed the higher moments M_5..M_10 (from the NM=1600 composite-Simpson OUTER grid) into the closed C_5, C_6, D_5, D_6 exponent-ladder brackets, but those moments never received an outer-truncation cross-check (imp-3603 covered only M_0..M_4). imp-3621 held the inner A(tau) rule identical on both paths and compared the imp-3600 outer-Simpson moments against an independent Gauss-Legendre outer reference (GL-24, 200 panels, self-converged to ~1e-15): the per-moment relative gap is ~1.31e-10 at M_5 and drops to the ~1e-15 rounding floor for M_6..M_10, more than an order of magnitude below the imp-3600 ~1e-9 fit tolerance, and the C_5/C_6/D_5/D_6 brackets match the GL-outer ones to << 1e-9 -- so the imp-3600 |p_fit-2| read-outs carry no residual outer-quadrature bias. Added a glossary entry recording this certification and the honest RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient scope (imp-3066 untouched, no QED). Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3649, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:18:35Z", category: "content", summary: "imp-3654 (content): add a glossary/concept entry for the imp-3623/imp-3625 dense-solver resolution of the N=2000 skew-Toeplitz third-pair Krylov artifact", files: ["src/data/glossary.js"], detail: "imp-3602 saw the third pair lambda_5=lambda_6 spread degrade from ~2e-14 to 1.01e-11 at N=2000 under a fixed m=440 Lanczos solve. imp-3623 cross-validated with an independent dense Householder+QL full-spectrum solver, finding the pair stays at machine precision (~1.18e-15) at N=2000 while sigma_2 agrees with Lanczos to ~2e-14. imp-3625 swept Krylov depth m in {440,480,560,640} and found the spread contracts from 1.01e-11 at m=440 to ~6e-15 at m>=480, with sigma_2 depth-invariant throughout. Added a glossary entry recording that the N=2000 loss is a Lanczos reorthogonalization artifact, not a genuine third-pair splitting. Content-only addition to src/data/glossary.js; no code logic changed.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3650, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:24:04Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3655 (ux): add a viz page of the imp-3617 self-consistent flow-gap residual ladder across the imp-3443 E_trunc floor grid", files: ["src/data/imp-3655-flow-gap-residual-ladder-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3655FlowGapResidualLadderViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "Adds a new visualization route /viz-imp3655-flow-gap-residual-ladder plotting, on a log axis across the imp-3443 half-to-double E_trunc floor grid f in {0.5,0.75,1.0,1.5,2.0}, four residual series baked from the imp-3617 floorGrid: the imp-3599 crude O(eps^2) model, the imp-3617 resummed leading term -d1 eps, the self-consistent O(eps^2) truncation, and the self-consistent O(eps^3) truncation, against a marked ~1e-13 exact-identity floor line. Confirms the geometric drop the imp-3617 module measured (e.g. at f=0.5: 4.49e-4 -> 6.54e-5 -> 1.38e-7 -> 3.13e-10 pp), with the O(eps^3) truncation beating the imp-3599 model by >=8.38e4x at the worst floor while still not reaching the exact floor (honest sub-gap imp-3617-fourthorder-fd-floor). Reference literals are baked into a lightweight viz-data module so the page imports no heavy bundle. Presentation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3651, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:31:20Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3656 (ux): add a viz page of the imp-3602/imp-3619 triple skew-Toeplitz gap ladder (-log rho, -log sigma_2, -log sigma_3) and the (j^2-1) amplitude-ratio signature", files: ["src/data/imp-3656-skew-toeplitz-triple-gap-ladder-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3656TripleSkewToeplitzGapLadderViz.jsx", "src/pages/Imp3611SkewToeplitzKrylovGapLadderViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "Adds a new visualization route /viz-imp3656-triple-skew-toeplitz-gap-ladder plotting, on a log-log axis across N=160..2000, the three skew-Toeplitz section gaps -log rho=-log(lambda_3/lambda_1), -log sigma_2=-log(lambda_5/lambda_1) (imp-3602), and -log sigma_3=-log(lambda_7/lambda_1) (imp-3619), all climbing toward the shared -2 section-gap exponent, plus a second panel showing the near-constant amplitude ratios -log sigma_2/-log rho and -log sigma_3/-log rho tending to the imp-3602/imp-3619 j^2-1 targets 8/3 and 5 (a_2:a_3:a_4 = 3:8:15). Reference literals are baked from the imp-3619 THIRD_GAP_LADDER (already cross-checked to < 3e-12 against imp-3602) into a lightweight viz-data module so the page imports no heavy bundle. Also adds a reciprocal Related link from the imp-3611 gap-ladder page. Presentation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3652, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:38:03Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3657 (ux): add a viz page of the imp-3620/imp-398 closed-form flow-factor pin at the sigma-crossover", files: ["src/data/imp-3657-sigma-crossover-tc-closedform-pin-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3657SigmaCrossoverTcClosedformPinViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "Adds a new visualization route /viz-imp3657-sigma-crossover-tc-closedform-pin with three panels baked from the imp-3604/imp-3620 floorGrid exports: a number-line chart showing the imp-398 t_c(N)~1/log gamma_N closed-form crossover-scale flow factor exp(C_G t_c(N_x)) landing at 22.05%..44.09% of the imp-3604 bracket [1,1.000474], strictly below the frozen imp-3580 node (a ~2.27x over-statement); a per-floor N_half/N_x ratio chart showing the value is now a single PINNED curve (0.997717..0.993128) rather than a bracket; and a log-scale bar chart comparing the imp-3620 residual C_G spread (<1e-6) against the imp-3604 flat-bracket spread (~3e-6) at each floor. Reference literals are baked into a lightweight viz-data module so the page imports no heavy bundle. Presentation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3653, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:44:34Z", category: "ux", summary: "imp-3658 (ux): add a viz page of the imp-3622 planted-replica argmax-drift discriminator", files: ["src/data/imp-3658-planted-replica-argmax-drift-viz-data.js", "src/pages/Imp3658PlantedReplicaArgmaxDriftViz.jsx", "src/App.jsx", "scripts/audit-nav-links.mjs"], detail: "Adds a new visualization route /viz-imp3658-planted-replica-argmax-drift with two panels baked from the imp-3622 measured export: a log-log argmax-vs-N chart showing the genuine planted feature (xi_true=250) staying pinned at every rung N in {1200,2400,4800,9600} while the first-fold (m=1) and second-fold (m=2) aliasing-replica argmaxes climb 2/4 xi_Nyq per doubling, both series sitting above the band ceiling xi_max=400 and the imp-3582 N_replica~764 clearance floor; and a bar chart of the across-ladder (N=1200 to 9600) argmax shift contrasting 0 (genuine) against ~8796.46 (first fold) and ~17592.92 (second fold, exactly 2x), the 0-vs-huge drift split the imp-3558 argmax-drift-0 discriminator relies on. Reference literals are baked into a lightweight viz-data module so the page imports no heavy bundle. Presentation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 untouched, NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3654, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:47:29Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3688 (numerical): dense-certify the SIXTH skew-Toeplitz pair lambda_11=lambda_12 at the deep rungs N in {1200,1600,2000}, extending the imp-3668 five-pair certification one level to the top-12", files: ["src/data/imp-3688-skew-toeplitz-sixth-pair-dense-crossval.js", "scripts/imp-3688-dense-sixth-pair-offline.mjs"], detail: "Extends the imp-3668 dense adjacent-pairing certification one spectrum level, computing the TOP-TWELVE Gram eigenvalues of the identical imp-3505/imp-3668 assembly Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025) with the SAME independent dense full-spectrum route (Householder tred1 + implicit-QL tql1: all eigenvalues, no Krylov subspace, no reorthogonalization) at the deep rungs. FINDING: the sixth pair lambda_11=lambda_12 is degenerate to relative < 6e-16 at every rung (3.95e-16/3.94e-16/5.90e-16), so the deep section spectrum is SIX-pair adjacent-paired; the sixth-pair amplitude sigma_5=lambda_11/lambda_1 climbs monotonically 0.99500 -> 0.99718 -> 0.99819 toward 1; and the dense top-10 here reproduce the imp-3668 baked deep top-10 to all printed digits (relative < 1e-13), confirming a faithful one-level extension of the same solve. Top-12 measured offline (N=2000 dense solve ~4.6 s) and baked; pairing/amplitude re-derived arithmetically at import (import-light). Pairing-STRUCTURE cross-check only; does NOT establish the sixth-pair amplitude LAW, does NOT construct the missing magnitude, imp-3066 positivity untouched. RH-EQUIVALENT, NO QED. Platt-Trudgian Lambda <= 0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3655, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:46:20Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3685 (numerical): extend the observable |p_fit-2| ladder past n=18 to n=40 and DETERMINE that the exact Laplace saddle tau*(n)^2 ratio plateaus while the crude (ln n)^2/n^3 ratio never does -- resolving sg-3670", files: ["src/data/imp-3685-fit-bias-saddle-plateau-n40.js"], detail: "Adds a self-computing measurement module extending the imp-3670 fit-bias ladder past its n=18 ceiling to n=40 on the SAME NM=1600 [0,6] Simpson moments (extended to M_48 for a four-term same-parity tail at every rung; grid/domain-converged to 12 sig figs at NM=3200 or T_A=7). Cross-checks reproduce the imp-3648 n=7 slope 1.9999953601 and imp-3667 n=9 slope 1.9999967140, and the observable law |p_fit-2|=|D_n|cov(a^2,ln a)/var(ln a) holds to <=1.1e-9 at every rung. CENTRAL findings: the naive (ln n)^2/n^3 ratio NEVER plateaus (still strictly climbing 2.5894e-4 to 1.0944e-3, ~4.2x at n=40), while the EXACT saddle ratio |p_fit-2|/|D_n^saddle| PLATEAUS toward covVar=0.0293884 from above (1.0711e-1 to 3.0106e-2; |D_n|/|D_n^saddle| falls 3.64422 to 1.02438), resolving the imp-3670 named residual sg-3670-lnn-saddle-not-asymptotic-at-n18. Residual sg-3685-saddle-subleading-Qn-correction-descends-past-n40: exact-saddle ratio still ~2.4% above covVar at n=40 (sub-leading Q_n/tau*^2-1), approached not reached. Measurement, RH-equivalent, necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 operator positivity untouched; no QED.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3656, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:51:05Z", category: "meta", summary: "imp-3659 (meta): audit whether the imp-3617/3618/3619/3620/3621/3622/3623/3624/3625 research modules are imported by any page/component consumer or are orphaned data files", files: ["src/data/imp-3659-3617-3625-cohort-module-surfacing-audit.js"], detail: "Continues the imp-3459/imp-3480/imp-3498/imp-3517/imp-3539/imp-3568/imp-3593/imp-3615/imp-3636 orphan-audit series to the imp-3617..imp-3625 cohort via the same transitive import-graph walk from src/pages and src/components. All nine raw module files are ORPHAN in the strict import-graph sense (consistent with the project convention that viz pages bake reference literals rather than importing research modules directly), but imp-3617/3619/3620 are already fully surfaced by proxy (dedicated glossary.js term + routed viz page each); imp-3618 and imp-3621 have a glossary term but no viz page (new viz tickets recommended); imp-3622 has a viz page but no glossary term (new glossary ticket recommended); imp-3623/imp-3624/imp-3625 are cross-validation/sensitivity/diagnostic utilities (the imp-3603 precedent) whose findings are consumed by downstream narrative modules, so they should stay intentionally-unwired. Read-only audit; no repair needed; no new bound; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3657, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:52:08Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3687 (numerical): close the imp-3668 sigma_4 amplitude-law deferral -- measure the FIFTH-pair amplitude sigma_4=lambda_9/lambda_1 across the full N=160..2000 ladder and confirm the j^2-1 amplitude law at pair j=5", files: ["src/data/imp-3687-skew-toeplitz-fifth-pair-amplitude-law.js", "scripts/imp-3687-fifth-pair-amplitude-ladder-offline.mjs"], detail: "imp-3668 dense-certified the fifth-pair lambda_9=lambda_10 degeneracy at the deep rungs only and EXPLICITLY DEFERRED the sigma_4 amplitude law to this ticket. Re-ran the identical imp-3505/imp-3619/imp-3668 skew-Toeplitz assembly Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) across the full imp-3555 ladder N in {160..2000} with the SAME independent dense full-spectrum route (Householder tred1 + implicit-QL tql1, no Krylov, no reorthogonalization; N=2000 ~5.0s offline) and extracted sigma_4=lambda_9/lambda_1. FINDINGS: (1) the fifth-pair gap ALSO converges to the -2 section-gap heuristic -- local log-log exponent of -log sigma_4 climbs monotonically -1.9588 (160-240) to -1.9948 (1600-2000), global fit q_4=-1.9822 (R^2=0.99999) matching the imp-3619 q_3=-1.9817 and q_1=-1.9811 to <1.2e-3; (2) the imp-3602/imp-3619 j^2-1 amplitude law (a_j proportional to j^2-1, a_5=24) holds at pair j=5 via THREE independent pair-ratios: -log sigma_4/-log rho -> 8.00021 = a_5/a_2 (mean 8.0060, spread <3e-2, monotone from above), -log sigma_4/-log sigma_2 -> 3.00006 = a_5/a_3, -log sigma_4/-log sigma_3 -> 1.60002 = a_5/a_4 = 8/5; (3) lambda_9=lambda_10 pairs to <3e-15 at every rung. Cross-checks: the three deep-rung sigma_4 reproduce the imp-3668 baked dense values exactly, and -log rho / -log sigma_2 / -log sigma_3 reproduce the imp-3619 baked Lanczos ladder to <3e-12 -- same converged spectrum. Literals baked offline, import-light, 9 self-checking assertions pass; build passes. MEASUREMENT only; does NOT construct the missing magnitude and does NOT attempt imp-3066 K_a>=0 positivity; RH-EQUIVALENT; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3658, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:52:54Z", category: "accuracy", summary: "imp-3689 (accuracy): assess whether the imp-3665 ~30% A(1) refinement shifts the imp-3646 C_n ~ (ln n)^2/(16 n^2) prefactor and D_n bias law, or is confined to the single autocorrelation magnitude", files: ["src/data/imp-3689-a1-refinement-moment-ratio-invariance.js"], detail: "The imp-3646 log-divergent leading coefficient C_n = M_(n+2)/((n+1)(n+2)M_n) and the bias coefficient D_n = C_(n+2)-C_n are built from moment RATIOS Q_n = M_(n+2)/M_n, so a tau-independent rescaling of the A-weight cancels. Recomputing Q_n on BOTH the exact imp-3646 coarse autocorr (n=1200 Simpson [0,7]) and an imp-3665-class refined autocorr (n=12000 [0,12]) over the same NM=1600 [0,6] moment reference reproduces the single-magnitude correction (A(1): 3.01e-75 -> 2.09e-75, ~30% drop) yet moves the moment ratios by only ~3e-6..1.6e-5 across n=3..18 (4-5 orders of magnitude below the 30% correction), so n^2 C_n is unchanged to imp-3646 printed 4 dp (0.0131 -> 0.1095), D_n to its printed 4 sig figs at every rung, and every law survives verbatim on the refined grid (Q_n and n^2 C_n strictly increasing, D_n < 0 with |D_n| strictly decreasing). CONFINED to the single autocorrelation magnitude: imp-3646 asymptotics stand. Self-computing measurement/stability-check, RH-equivalent, necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 operator positivity untouched; no QED. Platt-Trudgian Lambda <= 0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3659, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:55:54Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3686 (numerical): close sg-3663-log-vs-sqrt-fixed-pair -- a fourth matched-pair anchor m*(2800)=620 on a refined 20-step Krylov grid disfavours sqrt and prefers log for the fixed lambda_5=lambda_6 depth law", files: ["src/data/imp-3686-n2800-refined-anchor-log-vs-sqrt.js", "scripts/compute-imp3686-n2800-refined-anchor.mjs"], detail: "imp-3663 obtained the matched-pair triple m*(1600)=360, m*(2000)=480, m*(2400)=560 for the FIXED lambda_5=lambda_6 third pair and ruled out linear, but could not separate log from sqrt (the ~2.4-unit RMS gap sat below the 40-step +/-20 grid). Re-ran the identical imp-3505/imp-3625/imp-3663 skew-Toeplitz Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) single full-reorthogonalization Lanczos to m=720 at N=2800 (U=70), reading top-6 Gram Ritz on a REFINED 20-step sub-depth grid. RESULT: m*(2800)=620, bracketed between m=600 (pair56=4.4e-8, converging) and m=620 (pair56=5.6e-14, plateau) at the imp-3663 1e-13 plateau threshold, so quantisation halved to +/-10 (the fixed 2e-14 floor is too strict at N=2800 where the noise plateau is ~2.6e-14). FINDINGS: (i) the four anchors 360/480/560/620 continue the concave deceleration Delta m 120->80->60 over equal Delta N=400, so LINEAR stays ruled out; (ii) four-anchor least-squares RMS ranks log~7.2 < sqrt~11.2 < linear~15.2, widening the log-vs-sqrt gap from ~2.4 to ~4.0; (iii) the measured 620 sits ~33 units BELOW the imp-3663 three-anchor sqrt extrapolation (652.8) -- more than 3x the refined half-step -- but only ~20 below the log extrapolation (639.9), so SQRT is DISFAVOURED and LOG PREFERRED, resolving sg-3663-log-vs-sqrt-fixed-pair for log; (iv) the observed increment ratios 1:0.667:0.500 decelerate steeper than pure sqrt (1:0.905:0.833) and steeper than pure log (1:0.816:0.690), so the true form is at least as concave as log and may saturate steeper -- named residual sg-3686-steeper-than-log-fixed-pair. The three imp-3663 anchors are IMPORTED (not re-baked). Measurement/fit only, self-computing, import-light, 8 tripwire assertions; no positivity, imp-3066 UNTOUCHED, RH-equivalent, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3660, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:57:26Z", category: "numerical", summary: "imp-3690 (numerical): measure and derive the subleading term of the imp-3665-confirmed super-exponential A-weight decay -ln A(tau) ~ pi e^{4 tau}", files: ["src/data/imp-3690-a-weight-superexp-subleading-correction.js"], detail: "imp-3665 confirmed -ln A(tau)/(pi e^{4 tau}) -> 1 and NOTED an unquantified positive subleading correction. This pins it. Define r(tau) = -ln A(tau) - pi e^{4 tau}; the exact substitution x = pi e^{4 tau}(e^{4 s}-1) reduces r to -ln int_0^inf G(x)dx with NO cancellation (G(x)=Phi(s(x))Q(x)/(4(pi e^{4 tau}+x)) is O(1) with an e^{-x} tail), so r is exact to ~1e-13 by XMAX/M doubling -- beating the ~1e-3-relative uniform-s-grid wall imp-3665 hit on -ln A ~ 9365. RESULT: r(tau) -> C_inf = -ln(pi Phi(0)/2) = 0.3542923 (a CONSTANT, with Phi(0)=sum_n (2 pi^2 n^4 - 3 pi n^2) e^{-pi n^2} ~ 0.4466969), leading correction (3/(2 pi)) e^{-2 tau} from the -3 pi n^2 e^{2u} amplitude sub-term (endpoint-Laplace at s=0), next term O(e^{-4 tau}). Measured across tau in {0.5..3}: r descends 0.61688 -> 0.35548 to C_inf and (r-C_inf) e^{2 tau} descends 0.7138 -> 0.4791 to 3/(2 pi)=0.4774648 from above; the two-term ansatz C_inf + (3/(2 pi)) e^{-2 tau} matches r to 2.2e-4 at tau=2, 3e-5 at tau=2.5, 4e-6 at tau=3 (residual shrinks ~e^2 per Delta tau=0.5, confirming O(e^{-4 tau})). Cross-check: reproduces the imp-3665 tau=0.5,1 residuals (0.6169, 0.4297) where its grid was adequate, and shows its tau=2 read of -2.24 was uniform-grid noise (true r(2)=+0.3633). 8 self-checking assertions pass, build passes. Measurement/derivation, RH-EQUIVALENT, necessary-but-not-sufficient; imp-3066 operator positivity untouched; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda <= 0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3662, timestamp: "2026-07-03T16:05:00Z", category: "bug", summary: "imp-3660 (bug): audit the imp-3617..imp-3625 cohort and its four routed viz-page consumers for inadvertent false-QED or RH-overclaim framing -- NO DRIFT found", files: ["src/data/imp-3660-3617-3625-cohort-honesty-audit.js"], detail: "Per the imp-3637/imp-3616/imp-3594 honesty-audit pattern, grepped each of the nine imp-3617..imp-3625 modules and the four routed viz pages the imp-3659 surfacing audit identified (Imp3655/Imp3656/Imp3657/Imp3658) for the mandatory honesty markers: measurement/derivation-only framing, RH-equivalent necessary-but-not-sufficient scope, the imp-3066 off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel K_a>=0 positivity marked UNTOUCHED, Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 cited as the rigorous SOTA, and absence of QED / unconditional-RH phrasing. All nine modules and all four pages already carry a compliant banner (verdict/scope/honestCaveat fields plus a build-time honesty-gate assertion); no drift or repair needed. Read-only audit; no pages fabricated, no new bound; NO QED.", model: "sonnet-4-6", channel: "sonnet" },
  { id: 3663, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:58:59Z", category: "proof", summary: "imp-3691 (proof): assess whether the imp-3671 k~8.76 half-floor scale bears on the E(N) bridge constants via the imp-3661 density-corrected flow factor, or is confined to the G6a shock-front regime", files: ["src/data/imp-3691-half-floor-scale-vs-en-bridge-assessment.js"], detail: "Frontier-direction assessment. The E(N) bridge constant is fed (imp-2564) by the collision-TIME scale t_c ~ 1/(2 V0), with V0 read at the SINGLE mesoscopic anchor y_star=4d (k=1, Gronwall floor 0.991); imp-3661 pins the density-corrected flow factor to 1.0000917, ~19.3% of the imp-3604 bracket, as a scalar with no strip-height descent. The imp-3671 half-floor crosses 1/2 at k_half~8.76 (y~0.457 d), 8.76x deeper than the bridge anchor and below the mean spacing d (k=4, floor 0.865). VERDICT: CONFINED to the G6a shock-front regime, NO bearing on the E(N) share, for three reasons: (R1) disjoint reading heights -- the bridge reads V0 only at k=1, the half-floor is a k~8.76 phenomenon (~11.4% of the anchor height); (R2) disjoint inputs -- the 19.3% occupancy is fixed by the density log ratio 0.3870 (no k), k_half by E_meso=0.009041 and the k^2 collapse (no density ratio), no shared parameter; (R3) gross incommensurability -- a half-floor-driven E(N) contraction would sit at floor 1/2 (50% lost) vs the bridge 0.991 (0.9% lost), a ~55x lost-contraction ratio that would swamp the measured share. This is imp-2520 negative-finding 1 and the imp-3671 (S2) obstruction: the nearest-pair/front regime is a different, Gronwall-vacuous scale. Import-light (pulls literals from the two sibling modules), 5 self-checking assertions pass, build passes. Assessment/derivation only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 positivity untouched, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3661, timestamp: "2026-07-03T15:58:28Z", category: "accuracy", summary: "imp-3692 (accuracy): independently verify the imp-3668 baked deep-rung dense TOP-10 (fifth-pair) Gram eigenvalue literals via Sturm-bisection extraction on a re-typed imp-3505 assembly (the imp-3669 pattern extended two spectrum levels)", files: ["src/data/imp-3692-dense-fifth-pair-independent-verify.js", "scripts/imp-3692-dense-fifth-pair-independent-verify.mjs"], detail: "imp-3669 independently reproduced the imp-3643 baked top-8 by Sturm bisection (worst 1.77e-15); imp-3668 then baked NEW deep-rung TOP-10 literals (the FIFTH pair lambda_9=lambda_10) from a one-off implicit-QL offline solve that had NOT been cross-checked by an independent extraction. scripts/imp-3692-dense-fifth-pair-independent-verify.mjs re-typed the imp-3505/imp-3575 Ttilde(u,v)=a(v-u)R (NPHI=10, H0=0.025, midpoint) from scratch, formed the Gram S=T^T T explicitly at N in {1200,1600,2000}, and extracted the top-10 by STURM-SEQUENCE BISECTION on the Householder tridiagonal (a routine entirely different from the imp-3668 EISPACK implicit-QL tql1). RESULT: every rung reproduces the imp-3668 baked denseTop10 to WORST relative 1.77e-15 (all ten eigenvalues at N=1200/1600/2000, machine precision; identical to the imp-3669 top-8 worst since the first eight literals coincide), and the INDEPENDENT fifth-pair spread pair910=|l9-l10|/l9 is 0 (all bits) at N=1200 and N=2000 and 3.93e-16 at N=1600, i.e. < 1e-15 everywhere -- CONFIRMING the imp-3668 machine-precision lambda_9=lambda_10 degeneracy from an entirely different extraction. The imp-3668 top-10 literals and the fifth-pair pairing are CONFIRMED; no transcription or offline-drift error in the two new fifth-pair entries the pending Lanczos sigma_4=lambda_9/lambda_1 amplitude ticket reads. Verification/measurement only; does NOT establish the fifth-pair amplitude LAW and does NOT touch imp-3066; RH-EQUIVALENT; NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. Build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" },
  { id: 3664, timestamp: "2026-07-03T16:14:00Z", category: "proof", summary: "imp-3693 (proof): route-scope whether ANY repo microscopic reading carries the (x-x_prime) x-difference structure imp-3671 obstruction S1 needs for the G6a shock-front Hoelder-1/2 modulus C_Lip -- YES, the per-characteristic gap field g_k=gamma_{k+1}-gamma_k (NOT the strip-sup V0) clears S1, but S2 survives so G6a stays open", files: ["src/data/imp-3693-microscopic-xdiff-route-scoping.js"], detail: "Scopes the three named candidate microscopic readings against imp-3671 obstruction S1 (V0 is a strip-sup scalar with no per-characteristic x-difference, the wrong TYPE for a spatial Hoelder-1/2 modulus). R1 the imp-3642 direct-Dyson flow field publishes only the strip-SUP scalar V0 and DISCARDS the per-particle x_k differences its own RK4 advances (S1-blocked at the reading level, structure latent); R2 the nearest-pair statistic B=min_k g_k is a single adjacent gap (right TYPE) but an EXTREMUM, one scalar per configuration supplying at most one modulus point not a profile; R3 the per-characteristic gap field g_k(t)=gamma_{k+1}-gamma_k with its exact ODE dg_k/dt=4/g_k-2 g_k S_k (dyson-collision-lower-bound imp-325 / dyson-monotonicity-proof imp-322) is x-RESOLVED -- each g_k is an (x_{k+1}-x_k) difference indexed by lattice position and the per-k collision time tau_c(k) is a candidate per-characteristic tau_c(x) field of exactly the TYPE C_Lip needs, so R3 CLEARS S1. VERDICT: YES the repo owns a right-TYPE object (the per-gap field, NOT V0), scoping the route to approach C_Lip; but clearing S1 is necessary not sufficient -- obstruction S2 (the collision sits at the Gronwall-vacuous nearest-pair scale g_k->0, y->0; imp-2520 negative-finding 1) survives on R3, so G6a_shock_lipschitz stays OPEN. Route-scoping/assessment only, RH-equivalent, imp-3066 K_a>=0 UNTOUCHED, NO QED; Platt-Trudgian Lambda<=0.2 stays SOTA. 4 build-time assertions pass, build passes.", model: "opus-4-8", channel: "api-pool" }